;∞ﬂΩ="‹ºö§§<:å–º»s´º.∏ñº45Ì<)®ƒºg¯Äºö§§º˜¥=¥˘ì;Ãˇ<¥≤ÇºH–"<˙¨ºY˚ø<IÜ<≠o˚∫	´2ºrº+iú<°∆ª.∏< º°^ﬁº¶dÇ<éØÃ;ftΩ≤M∫@ Ω…∞Ω‘hª∆ºr˜Ü<©KÕº˙,ºt°nºjﬂÀ<û6º√’∂<ï—µ:"?J=©Ω™:˜¥ºl†#<[uΩ»}Ÿ<V#ΩV¨Eºò*ﬁ<òqoºX&åªñ«<yjØ;Ø[ü<€iN<@Ÿ=∞æıªŸ¶º)"<P«ø;Eá<5‰≠:7·<Ag(<t	û<@∏g;ÿå±∫ß´ì;⁄€+ºÊh‘=\∏º-ÌΩ.PÁ;Z™␀ºÉs„ºÀÂº√»º‘␀‘<àX<¥≤=;s<çìº∫ËG<ßC‰ºπ°6ºøIŸº%=Ö:§<õ(;␀Èè<éhªªí;™ºG‰˛;›„îºiQ)º”+ Ω˜âCΩ¬ﬂ‰:òqo<Éi5Ωí”˙ºp6Ø<Ôú‘∫‰ùN;ø±à<ˇ´¨∫≠o˚º¥¬ºáÑ=âXiª!jΩ§≠ÿ;ft=WÈ(ºæª∂<7ÑÁª≥∫whºo®<ÄªºUΩ∂´<‚D&=◊OŒª»}YºâXÈº0Éú;É∫Ù<*ûºJrº.	VºŸ…îªLf<IÜ<{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA:Short-chain fatty acids (SCFA) are fermentation products derived from dietary fiber, playing significant roles in energy metabolism and the reduction of inflammation. They are produced during the fermentation process of dietary fiber by the intestinal microbiota, highlighting their importance in gut health and overall metabolic functions."}{"title": "ESCUDERO \u00c1LVAREZ E:Escudero \u00c1lvarez E is an author who contributed to the research on dietary fiber and its implications in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "GUARNER AGUILAR F:Guarner Aguilar F is an author who contributed to the research on probiotics, prebiotics, and symbiotics in clinical practice."}{"title": "FALLO INTESTINAL:Fallo intestinal, or intestinal failure, is defined as a condition characterized by a significant reduction in intestinal function, falling below the minimum threshold necessary for the adequate absorption of macronutrients, water, and electrolytes. This impairment necessitates intravenous supplementation to maintain health and support growth. In essence, individuals with intestinal failure are unable to absorb sufficient nutrients through their intestines, which leads to the requirement for nutritional support to ensure their well-being."}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdA ASOCIADA A NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL:Liver damage associated with home parenteral nutrition, which can occur due to various factors related to intestinal failure."}{"title": "ILEOSTOM\u00cdA:A surgical procedure that creates an opening in the abdominal wall for waste to exit the body, often leading to significant fluid loss."}{"title": "VIDAL CASARIEGO:Vidal Casariego is a medical professional who co-authored the guidelines on short bowel syndrome and its management."}{"title": "HIPOCLACEMIA:Hypocalcemia is a condition characterized by low calcium levels in the blood. It can be associated with vitamin D deficiency, which is essential for calcium absorption. Additionally, hypocalcemia may occur in patients with chronic kidney disease, where it is often related to phosphorus levels. This condition highlights the interconnectedness of calcium, vitamin D, and kidney function in maintaining overall mineral balance in the body."}{"title": "DENSITOMETR\u00cdAS:DENSITOMETR\u00cdAS refers to the practice of conducting bone density tests periodically to assess the health of bones, particularly in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. These tests are essential for monitoring the effects of parenteral nutrition on bone health, ensuring that any potential issues can be identified and addressed in a timely manner."}{"title": "T-SCORE:T-SCORE is a measurement utilized in bone density tests to evaluate bone health. It serves as a comparative metric, assessing an individual's bone density against that of a healthy 30-year-old. Lower T-scores indicate a higher risk of osteoporosis, making it a crucial tool in diagnosing osteoporosis, particularly in patients with specific conditions such as FQ (cystic fibrosis)."}{"title": "PTHI:Parathyroid hormone levels that can indicate calcium metabolism issues, often monitored in patients with vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "CALCEMIA:The level of calcium in the blood, which is crucial for diagnosing conditions related to bone health and vitamin D status."}{"title": "OSTEOMALACIA:OSTEOMALACIA is a condition characterized by the softening of bones, primarily due to a prolonged deficiency of vitamin D, which affects calcium absorption and leads to weakened bones. This condition can manifest in various contexts, including in patients with Wilson's disease and those receiving home parenteral nutrition. Osteomalacia results in symptoms such as bone pain and overall weakness, and it involves the deterioration of bone matrix mineralization, contributing to the fragility of the skeletal structure."}{"title": "REYES GARC\u00cdA:Reyes Garc\u00eda is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "J\u00d3DAR GIMENO:J\u00f3dar Gimeno is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA MART\u00cdN:Garc\u00eda Mart\u00edn is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "ROMERO MU\u00d1OZ:Romero Mu\u00f1oz is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ S\u00c1EZ:G\u00f3mez S\u00e1ez is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "LUQUE FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Luque Fern\u00e1ndez is one of the authors of the clinical practice guidelines for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis associated with endocrine and nutritional diseases."}{"title": "GRUPO DE METABOLISMO MINERAL:The Grupo de Metabolismo Mineral is a group within the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n focused on mineral metabolism and its clinical implications."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N GLOBAL SUBJETIVA GENERADA POR EL PACIENTE:The Valoraci\u00f3n Global Subjetiva Generada por el Paciente (VGS-GP) is a subjective assessment tool used to evaluate nutritional status, particularly in oncology patients."}{"title": "MINI-NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT:The Mini-Nutritional Assessment (MNA) is a screening tool used to identify patients at risk of malnutrition."}{"title": "DUODENOPANCREATECTOM\u00cdA:Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of the duodenum and a portion of the pancreas. This operation is often performed in cases of pancreatic cancer or gastric cancer, making it a critical intervention for patients suffering from these conditions. The procedure can lead to complications such as diabetes and malabsorption, which are important considerations in the management of patients post-surgery. Overall, duodenopancreatectomy is utilized primarily in the treatment of pancreatic diseases, highlighting its significance in surgical oncology."}{"title": "ERAS SOCIETY:The ERAS Society is an organization dedicated to enhancing perioperative care, with a particular emphasis on improved recovery following surgery. It provides comprehensive guidelines aimed at optimizing surgical recovery processes. Among its recommendations, the ERAS Society specifically addresses the needs of patients undergoing pancreaticoduodenectomy, ensuring that best practices are implemented to facilitate better outcomes in surgical recovery."}{"title": "K. LASSEN:K. Lassen es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas para el cuidado perioperatorio en la cirug\u00eda pancre\u00e1tica, contribuyendo a la investigaci\u00f3n en nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica."}{"title": "GASTROYEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA:La gastroyeyunostom\u00eda es un procedimiento quir\u00fargico que conecta el est\u00f3mago con el yeyuno, utilizado en el contexto de la cirug\u00eda pancre\u00e1tica."}{"title": "DRENES:Los drenajes son dispositivos utilizados para eliminar fluidos del cuerpo despu\u00e9s de una cirug\u00eda, en este caso, tras la duodenopancreatectom\u00eda."}{"title": "DEHISCENCIA DE ANASTOMOSIS:DEHISCENCIA DE ANASTOMOSIS refers to anastomotic dehiscence, which is a complication that occurs post-surgery. This condition indicates a failure of the surgical connection between two segments of the intestine, leading to a separation of the anastomosis. It is a significant concern in surgical procedures involving intestinal reconnections, as it can result in serious complications for the patient."}{"title": "MJ:MJ is an author who contributed to the chapter on nutrition in surgical patients in the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'."}{"title": "RAM\u00cdREZ RODR\u00cdGUEZ JM:Ram\u00edrez Rodr\u00edguez JM is an author who contributed to the chapter on nutrition in surgical patients in the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'."}{"title": "GIMENO ORNA JA:Gimeno Orna JA is an author who contributed to the chapter on nutrition in surgical patients in the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN PACIENTE QUIR\u00daRGICO:A chapter in the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n' discussing nutrition in surgical patients."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS DEL TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL SUPERIOR:Neoplasias del tracto gastrointestinal superior refers to cancers affecting the upper gastrointestinal tract, which are discussed in the context of perioperative nutrition in the chapter."}{"title": "COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD:COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD refers to a comprehensive analysis used to evaluate the economic viability of various interventions aimed at achieving specific health outcomes. This analysis measures effectiveness in clinical terms, such as the cost per case of infections or the cost of life years gained. It plays a crucial role in the economic evaluation of enteral nutrition formulas, particularly highlighting their benefits for surgical patients. Additionally, coste-efectividad is essential for assessing the economic feasibility of home artificial nutrition within healthcare systems. It is also a significant factor when choosing between parenteral and enteral nutrition, as the costs associated with devices and care are generally higher for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS:\"COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS\" refers to infectious complications that can arise in surgical patients, particularly in those with cancer. These complications are significant adverse effects that may occur post-surgery and are often addressed in the context of nutritional support. One specific risk associated with these complications is lipoid pneumonia due to aspiration, which can be linked to the ketogenic diet. To mitigate the health issues that may arise after surgery, the use of immunomodulatory formulas is recommended. Overall, \"COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS\" encompasses a range of infectious risks that necessitate careful management and nutritional strategies to improve patient outcomes."}{"title": "PEDRO JOS\u00c9 PIN\u00c9S CORRALES:Pedro Jos\u00e9 Pin\u00e9s Corrales is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the University Hospital Complex of Albacete and an associate professor at the Faculty of Medicine of Albacete, University of Castilla-La Mancha."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE CASTILLA-LA MANCHA:The University of Castilla-La Mancha is an educational institution where Pedro Jos\u00e9 Pin\u00e9s Corrales serves as an associate professor in Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "ACAD\u00c9MIA CTO-MEDICINA:The CTO-Medicine Academy is an educational institution where Pedro Jos\u00e9 Pin\u00e9s Corrales teaches Endocrinology, Metabolism, and Nutrition."}{"title": "ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA:Adrenoleucodistrofia, also known as adrenoleukodystrophy, is a hereditary genetic disorder that affects lipid metabolism, specifically the metabolism of very long-chain fatty acids. This condition is characterized by the abnormal accumulation of these fatty acids in the body, which primarily impacts the myelin sheath of the nervous system and the adrenal cortex. As a result, individuals with adrenoleucodistrofia experience a range of neurological decline and various metabolic issues, including problems related to the adrenal glands.\n\nThe disorder is notable for its variable phenotypic expression, meaning that symptoms can differ significantly among affected individuals. It is relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases due to its overlapping symptoms. Management of adrenoleucodistrofia often requires dietary interventions to help mitigate the effects of the disorder. Overall, adrenoleucodistrofia represents a complex interplay of genetic and metabolic factors that necessitate careful clinical attention."}{"title": "CYP21A2:CYP21A2 is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the production of 21-hydroxylase, and its deficiency can lead to primary adrenal insufficiency. This condition is particularly significant in young males who exhibit symptoms of adrenal insufficiency. The diagnosis of adrenal insufficiency often involves the detection of antibodies related to CYP21A2, highlighting its importance in clinical assessments. Additionally, the gene CYP21A2 is responsible for encoding the enzyme, and its deficiency is a known cause of congenital adrenal hyperplasia."}{"title": "HOSPITAL COMPLEJO UNIVERSITARIO DE ALBACETE:The Hospital Complex of Albacete is a healthcare facility where various medical specialties, including Endocrinology, are practiced."}{"title": "ANEMIA PERNICIOSA:Anemia perniciosa is an autoimmune condition characterized by impaired absorption of vitamin B12. This disorder can be associated with various other autoimmune diseases, including autoimmune thyroid diseases and type 1 diabetes mellitus. Additionally, it is frequently linked to primary adrenal insufficiency."}{"title": "GEN X-ALD:The GEN X-ALD gene is responsible for encoding a protein that functions as a peroxisomal membrane transporter, specifically involved in the transport of fatty acids within cells. Mutations in the X-ALD gene result in a condition known as adrenoleukodystrophy, which is characterized by the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids due to impaired transport. This genetic alteration can lead to severe neurological and adrenal dysfunction, highlighting the critical role of the X-ALD gene in cellular fatty acid metabolism."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME PLURIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 2:El s\u00edndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2 es una condici\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica que se caracteriza por la presencia de m\u00faltiples enfermedades autoinmunitarias, incluyendo insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria."}{"title": "HLA-DR3:HLA-DR3 is a genetic region that is associated with type 2 autoimmune polyglandular syndrome, as well as other autoimmune diseases. It is classified as a histocompatibility antigen, playing a significant role in the immune system's response."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO 1:Diabetes tipo 1 es una enfermedad cr\u00f3nica que afecta la forma en que el cuerpo metaboliza la glucosa, resultando en niveles elevados de glucosa en sangre. Esta condici\u00f3n es una enfermedad autoinmunitaria, en la cual el sistema inmunol\u00f3gico ataca las c\u00e9lulas productoras de insulina en el p\u00e1ncreas, lo que lleva a la incapacidad del cuerpo para producir insulina. Como resultado, los pacientes con diabetes tipo 1 requieren un manejo y tratamiento de por vida para controlar sus niveles de glucosa en sangre.\n\nAdem\u00e1s, la diabetes tipo 1 es un \u00e1rea principal de investigaci\u00f3n para Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez, quien se enfoca en su tratamiento y gesti\u00f3n. Tambi\u00e9n se ha observado que la diabetes tipo 1 puede tener una mayor prevalencia entre pacientes con trastornos alimentarios, como la Anorexia Nerviosa. Aunque menos frecuentemente, esta enfermedad puede estar asociada con el s\u00edndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2."}{"title": "FALLO OV\u00c1RICO PRECOZ:El fallo ov\u00e1rico precoz es una condici\u00f3n que puede estar asociada con el s\u00edndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2, afectando la funci\u00f3n reproductiva en mujeres j\u00f3venes."}{"title": "HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA:\"Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna\" is a comprehensive medical textbook edited by a team of experts including Kasper DL, Hauser SL, Jameson JL, Fauci AS, Longo DL, and Loscazo J. This authoritative reference provides extensive information on various aspects of internal medicine, covering a wide range of medical conditions and treatments. Notably, it includes detailed discussions on adrenal disorders, such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia and pheochromocytoma, as well as other endocrine disorders. The textbook is widely recognized and utilized in the medical field for its thorough guidelines and insights into internal medicine, making it an essential resource for healthcare professionals."}{"title": "ENDOCRINE SOCIETY:The Endocrine Society is a professional organization dedicated to advancing research and education in the field of endocrinology. It plays a crucial role in establishing clinical practice guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of various endocrine disorders. These guidelines encompass a wide range of conditions, including adrenal insufficiency, primary aldosteronism, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, pheochromocytoma, paraganglioma, and hypoglycemic disorders. \n\nAdditionally, the Endocrine Society provides specific guidelines for the treatment and management of gender-dysphoric individuals, as well as for conditions such as hirsutism. The organization is committed to ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest evidence-based practices for the effective management of endocrine disorders, thereby improving patient care and outcomes. \n\nIn summary, the Endocrine Society serves as a vital resource for clinicians, offering comprehensive guidelines that address a broad spectrum of endocrine conditions, thereby enhancing the quality of care in this specialized field."}{"title": "SOX3:A gene associated with certain rare causes of adrenal insufficiency."}{"title": "ALDOSTERONA:Aldosterona, also known as aldosterone, is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium and potassium levels in the body. It is particularly relevant in the context of adrenal disorders and is involved in the evaluation of adrenal masses. Aldosterona functions by increasing sodium retention, which in turn helps to regulate blood pressure and maintain fluid balance. Its secretion is often elevated in conditions such as obesity, highlighting its impact on blood pressure regulation. Additionally, a deficiency in aldosterone is linked to primary adrenal insufficiency, underscoring its importance in overall electrolyte balance and cardiovascular health. The hormone activates mineralocorticoid receptors, further contributing to its role in sodium retention and blood pressure management."}{"title": "POMC:Proopiomelanocortin (POMC) is a precursor polypeptide that plays a crucial role in the production of several important hormones. When mutated, POMC can lead to isolated adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) deficiency, which can have significant physiological implications."}{"title": "TBX19:A gene that, when mutated, can cause isolated ACTH deficiency, affecting adrenal function."}{"title": "ADRENALITIS AUTOINMUNITARIA:"}{"title": "TAC CRANEAL:La TAC craneal es un procedimiento de imagen utilizado para diagnosticar condiciones relacionadas con el cerebro, incluyendo tumores que pueden causar el s\u00edndrome de Cushing."}{"title": "PACIENTE DE 56 A\u00d1OS:Una paciente de 56 a\u00f1os que presenta s\u00edntomas compatibles con el s\u00edndrome de Cushing, incluyendo aumento de peso, equimosis y hipertensi\u00f3n arterial."}{"title": "WILLIAMS TEXTBOOK OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology\" is a comprehensive medical textbook edited by Melmed S, Polonsky KS, Larsen PR, and Kronenberg HM. It serves as a key reference in the field of endocrinology, providing detailed information on a wide range of endocrine disorders and their treatments. The textbook covers various aspects of endocrinology, including physiological processes and specific disorders such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, pheochromocytoma, and osteoporosis. Additionally, it addresses pediatric disorders of sex development and the role of vitamin D in health. The \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology\" is recognized for its thorough exploration of hormonal disorders, making it an essential resource for medical professionals and students in the field."}{"title": "COLLESTEROL DESMOLASE:Cholesterol desmolase is an enzyme that catalyzes the first step of steroidogenesis, converting cholesterol into pregnenolone, and is stimulated by ACTH."}{"title": "KASPER DL:Kasper DL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, particularly noted for his contributions to the medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.\" This comprehensive work includes extensive information on various adrenal disorders, such as Cushing's syndrome, hyperaldosteronism, and congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Kasper DL's expertise is highlighted in the context of disorders of the adrenal cortex, making significant contributions to the understanding and treatment of these conditions. His role as an editor and contributor to this influential textbook underscores his importance in the medical community, particularly in the study and management of adrenal disorders."}{"title": "MUJER DE 72 A\u00d1OS:A 72-year-old woman presenting with symptoms of Cushing's syndrome and a tumor in the right lung."}{"title": "PARANEOPLASTIC SYNDROME:Paraneoplastic syndrome refers to a set of symptoms that occur in patients with cancer, which in this case is likely related to the tumor causing Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "MITOTAN:Mitotan is a medication used primarily in the treatment of adrenal carcinoma, which also inhibits steroidogenesis and has adrenolytic effects."}{"title": "METOPIRONA:Metopirona, also known as Metopirone, is a medication that primarily functions as an inhibitor of 11-\u03b2-hydroxylase. This action results in a rapid decrease in cortisol levels, making it particularly useful in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "HARRISON PRINCIPLES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE:The \"Harrison Principles of Internal Medicine\" is a comprehensive medical textbook that provides extensive information on a wide range of medical conditions. Notably, it covers adrenal disorders, including Cushing's syndrome, and includes detailed discussions on various conditions related to the adrenal cortex. This textbook serves as a vital resource for understanding complex medical issues and is widely recognized in the field of internal medicine."}{"title": "ADRENAL CORTEX:"}{"title": "MEXICO DF:Mexico DF is the capital of Mexico, where the Spanish edition of Harrison Principles of Internal Medicine was published."}{"title": "MULTICENTER RANDOMIZED STUDY:A multicenter randomized study that evaluated the effects of treatments on cortisol levels in patients with Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "PETROSAL SINUS CATHETERIZATION:Petrosal sinus catheterization is a diagnostic procedure used to determine the source of ACTH in patients suspected of having Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "HYPERCORTISOLISM:HYPERCORTISOLISM is a condition characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body. This condition is often associated with Cushing's syndrome, which presents a range of symptoms linked to the elevated cortisol levels. Hypercortisolism is recognized as a hallmark of Cushing's syndrome, highlighting its significance in the diagnosis and understanding of this endocrine disorder."}{"title": "ADRENAL GLANDS:The adrenal glands are endocrine glands that produce hormones, including cortisol, and are involved in Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "SOMATOSTATIN ANALOGS:"}{"title": "ADENOMA:ADENOMA refers to a benign tumor of glandular origin that can occur in various glands, including the adrenal glands, parathyroid glands, and pituitary gland. In the adrenal glands, adenomas are characterized by their lipid content and are often detected through imaging techniques. These tumors may be associated with incidental findings during imaging studies. In the parathyroid glands, adenomas can lead to primary hyperparathyroidism, resulting in elevated calcium levels in the blood (hypercalcemia). Additionally, adenomas in the pituitary gland can cause conditions such as Cushing's syndrome due to excessive production of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). Overall, adenomas are benign tumors that can have significant clinical implications depending on their location and the hormones they may affect."}{"title": "SUPRARENAL GLANDS:The adrenal glands are responsible for producing hormones like cortisol and androgens, and can be affected in cases of Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "GADOLINIUM:Gadolinium is a contrast agent used in MRI scans to enhance the visibility of structures, which is important in diagnosing conditions like Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "HAUSER SL:Hauser SL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, recognized for his contributions to the medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.\" He has collaborated on topics related to adrenal cortex disorders, including congenital adrenal hyperplasia and Cushing's syndrome, providing valuable insights into these medical conditions. Additionally, Hauser SL has played a significant role in enhancing the understanding of pheochromocytoma through his editorial work. His expertise and contributions have made him a notable figure in the literature surrounding internal medicine."}{"title": "JAMESON JL:Jameson JL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, known for his significant contributions to the medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.\" This comprehensive work includes critical information on various endocrine disorders, such as adrenal cortex disorders, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, and pheochromocytoma. Jameson JL's expertise and involvement in the writing and editing of this influential text highlight his role in advancing medical education and knowledge in internal medicine."}{"title": "FAUCI AS:Fauci AS is a notable author and editor in the field of internal medicine, recognized for his contributions to the esteemed medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.\" He has played a significant role in discussing various medical conditions, including adrenal cortex disorders, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, and pheochromocytoma. His work is frequently referenced in the context of these conditions, highlighting his expertise and influence in the field of infectious diseases and internal medicine."}{"title": "LONGO DL:Longo DL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, recognized for his contributions to the esteemed medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine.\" This comprehensive work addresses a wide range of medical conditions, including disorders related to the adrenal cortex, such as Cushing's syndrome and congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Longo DL's expertise is reflected in his editorial role, where he collaborates with other experts to provide in-depth information on various medical topics, including pheochromocytoma. His involvement in this influential reference underscores his significant impact on the field of internal medicine."}{"title": "LOSCASO J:Loscaso J is an author and contributor to Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, providing information on various medical conditions including Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "MICROADENOMAS:"}{"title": "ETOMIDATE:Etomidate is an intravenous anesthetic that suppresses adrenal cortisol synthesis, used in urgent clinical situations to lower cortisol levels."}{"title": "TRILOSTANE:Trilostane is a medication that blocks the synthesis of adrenal steroid hormones, indicated for treating hyperadrenocorticism in dogs."}{"title": "TRILOSTANO:Trilostano is a medication that blocks the synthesis of adrenal steroid hormones, indicated for the treatment of hyperadrenocorticism in dogs due to Cushing's disease."}{"title": "MITOTANO:Mitotano is a medication primarily used for the symptomatic treatment of advanced adrenal carcinoma, specifically in cases that are inoperable, metastatic, or recurrent. It functions by inhibiting several enzymes involved in steroidogenesis and exhibits adrenolytic effects. Additionally, Mitotano can induce the enzyme CYP3A4, which may influence the metabolism of other drugs. This multifaceted approach makes Mitotano a critical option in managing advanced adrenocortical carcinoma."}{"title": "LOSCAZO J:Loscazo J is a notable author and editor in the field of internal medicine. He is mentioned in references concerning disorders of the adrenal cortex, highlighting his contributions to the understanding of these medical conditions. Loscazo J has played a significant role in the book \"Principles of Internal Medicine,\" where he addresses topics such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Additionally, he serves as an editor for the esteemed medical textbook \"Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine,\" where he has contributed to the sections on pheochromocytoma and has been actively involved in the broader medical literature and research related to internal medicine."}{"title": "HORMONAS ESTEROIDES:HORMONAS ESTEROIDES son un grupo de hormonas que incluyen la aldosterona y el cortisol. Estas hormonas desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n de diversas funciones en el cuerpo."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT:La enfermedad de McCune-Albright es causada por mutaciones som\u00e1ticas en el GNAS, que afectan la regulaci\u00f3n de la prote\u00edna Gs\u03b1 y el AMPc."}{"title": "GL\u00c1NDULAS SUPRARRENALES:The \"GL\u00c1NDULAS SUPRARRENALES,\" or adrenal glands, are vital organs responsible for the production of various hormones, including androgens such as dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) and cortisol. These glands play a significant role in the endocrine system and are involved in several physiological processes. In particular, the production of androgens by the adrenal glands can contribute to hyperandrogenism, a condition often observed in polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS). Additionally, the bilateral growth of the adrenal glands can serve as a diagnostic indicator for Cushing's syndrome, a disorder characterized by excessive cortisol production. Furthermore, the adrenal glands are also the site where pheochromocytomas, tumors that can affect hormone production, may occur, which are associated with mutations in the RET gene. Overall, the adrenal glands are crucial for hormone regulation and can be implicated in various medical conditions."}{"title": "TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS PANCRE\u00c1TICOS:Los tumores neuroendocrinos pancre\u00e1ticos son una causa de secreci\u00f3n ect\u00f3pica de ACTH, que puede contribuir al s\u00edndrome de Cushing."}{"title": "CARCINOMAS DE C\u00c9LULAS PEQUE\u00d1AS PULMONARES:Los carcinomas de c\u00e9lulas peque\u00f1as pulmonares pueden causar s\u00edndrome de Cushing por producci\u00f3n ect\u00f3pica de ACTH."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA GS\u0391:La prote\u00edna Gs\u03b1 es una prote\u00edna reguladora que juega un papel crucial en la se\u00f1alizaci\u00f3n celular y est\u00e1 implicada en la enfermedad de McCune-Albright."}{"title": "LITERATURA REVISADA:La literatura revisada se refiere a la informaci\u00f3n actualizada sobre el s\u00edndrome de Cushing, que se encuentra en fuentes como UpToDate."}{"title": "GLANDULAS SUPRARRENALES:Las gl\u00e1ndulas suprarrenales son \u00f3rganos que producen hormonas, incluyendo cortisol, y su crecimiento bilateral puede ser diagn\u00f3stico del s\u00edndrome de Cushing."}{"title": "MUTACIONES SOM\u00c1TICAS:"}{"title": "GLUCOCORTICOIDS:Glucocorticoids are a class of steroid hormones that play a significant role in the regulation of metabolism and immune response. However, when used long-term or excessively, glucocorticoids can lead to osteoporosis, a condition characterized by weakened bones. This adverse effect occurs due to their impact on calcium absorption and bone formation, making individuals more susceptible to bone density loss. Additionally, resistance to glucocorticoids can result in various clinical conditions, highlighting the importance of careful management of these medications."}{"title": "DEXAMETHASONE:Dexamethasone is a synthetic glucocorticoid and corticosteroid medication utilized in the diagnosis and treatment of various medical conditions. It is commonly employed in tests to suppress cortisol production, aiding in the diagnosis of conditions such as Cushing syndrome. Additionally, Dexamethasone is used to differentiate between functional and tumor-related causes of hyperandrogenism. Its therapeutic applications include the treatment of Cushing's syndrome, where it works to suppress adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) levels. Overall, Dexamethasone plays a significant role in both diagnostic and therapeutic settings related to hormonal disorders."}{"title": "RESISTENCIA TISULAR A GLUCOCORTICOIDES:Tissue resistance to glucocorticoids is a condition where the body's tissues do not respond effectively to glucocorticoid hormones, leading to clinical symptoms of excess hormones."}{"title": "MUTACIONES EN EL DOMINIO DE FIJACI\u00d3N A LOS ESTEROIDES:Mutations in the steroid-binding domain can affect the function of glucocorticoid receptors, leading to resistance to glucocorticoids."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE BARTTER:El s\u00edndrome de Bartter es un defecto gen\u00e9tico raro que se manifiesta como un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo, afectando espec\u00edficamente a la porci\u00f3n gruesa del asa ascendente de Henle en los ri\u00f1ones. Este s\u00edndrome se caracteriza por la presencia de hipopotasemia (bajos niveles de potasio en sangre) y alcalosis metab\u00f3lica, junto con niveles elevados de renina y aldosterona. A pesar de estas alteraciones, no se presenta hipertensi\u00f3n. La condici\u00f3n resulta en un hiperaldosteronismo hiperrenin\u00e9mico, que es consecuencia de la p\u00e9rdida de sodio y cloro a nivel renal."}{"title": "DIABETES MAL CONTROLADA:La diabetes mal controlada puede estar asociada con hipercortisolismo fisiol\u00f3gico y caracter\u00edsticas del s\u00edndrome de Cushing."}{"title": "PHILADELPHIA:Philadelphia is a city in Pennsylvania, USA, renowned for its historical significance and its prominent medical institutions. It serves as the location for Elsevier, the publisher of the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, which provides essential guidelines and information on endocrine disorders. Additionally, Philadelphia is noted for its role in medical publishing, being home to other notable publishers such as Lippincott-Raven and WB Saunders Company, which published works like \"Enteral and Tube Feeding.\" Overall, Philadelphia is recognized not only for its rich history but also as a key hub for medical literature and publishing in the United States."}{"title": "ADENOMA SUPRARRENAL:Adenoma suprarrenal is a benign tumor of the adrenal gland that can produce aldosterone, leading to conditions such as Cushing's syndrome and hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISM FAMILIAR TIPO 1:Familial hyperaldosteronism type 1 is an autosomal dominant hereditary syndrome that causes excessive aldosterone production due to a genetic mutation."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISM FAMILIAR TIPO 2:Familial hyperaldosteronism type 2 is a hereditary condition characterized by hyperaldosteronism without suppression by dexamethasone, often indistinguishable from primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISM:Hyperaldosteronism is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of aldosterone, a hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating blood pressure and electrolyte balance. This condition often arises due to an adrenal adenoma or hyperplasia, which are abnormalities in the adrenal glands. As a result of the elevated aldosterone levels, individuals with hyperaldosteronism typically experience hypertension (high blood pressure) and may also have electrolyte imbalances, particularly low renin levels in the blood."}{"title": "HIPERALDOSTERONISMO FAMILIAR TIPO 3:HIPERALDOSTERONISMO FAMILIAR TIPO 3 es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico dominante caracterizado por un fenotipo agresivo que se manifiesta a trav\u00e9s de hipertensi\u00f3n grave y resistente al tratamiento desde la infancia. Esta condici\u00f3n es causada por mutaciones en el gen KCNJ5, el cual codifica el canal de potasio Kir 3.4."}{"title": "KCNJ5:El gen KCNJ5 codifica el canal de potasio Kir 3.4, cuya mutaci\u00f3n est\u00e1 relacionada con el hiperaldosteronismo familiar tipo 3."}{"title": "SEUDOHIPOALDOSTERONISMO:SEUDOHIPOALDOSTERONISMO, or pseudohypoaldosteronism, is a condition defined by the body's resistance to the action of mineralocorticoids, particularly aldosterone. This resistance results in a syndrome characterized by salt-wasting, which manifests as hyponatremia (low sodium levels) and hyperkalemia (high potassium levels), despite the presence of elevated levels of both aldosterone and renin in the bloodstream. The symptoms associated with SEUDOHIPOALDOSTERONISMO are similar to those observed in hypoaldosteronism, highlighting the condition's impact on electrolyte balance and fluid regulation in the body."}{"title": "NR3C2:El gen NR3C2 codifica el receptor de los mineralocorticoides, y su mutaci\u00f3n est\u00e1 asociada con el seudohipoaldosteronismo renal tipo 1."}{"title": "SUPRARRENALES:Las suprarrenales son gl\u00e1ndulas que producen hormonas, y su disfunci\u00f3n puede estar relacionada con trastornos como el hiperaldosteronismo y el seudohipoaldosteronismo."}{"title": "RENINA:RENINA is an enzyme produced by the kidneys that plays a crucial role in the regulation of blood pressure and fluid balance. It is significant in the evaluation of adrenal disorders, as its secretion is influenced by various factors, including the levels of deoxycorticosterone acetate (DOCA), with higher DOCA levels leading to decreased renin secretion. Overall, RENINA is essential for maintaining cardiovascular health and homeostasis in the body."}{"title": "ENAC:El canal de sodio sensible a amilorida (ENaC) es un canal i\u00f3nico que regula la reabsorci\u00f3n de sodio en los ri\u00f1ones y est\u00e1 implicado en trastornos como el seudohipoaldosteronismo."}{"title": "STEWART PM:Stewart PM is a distinguished medical professional and researcher known for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly regarding the adrenal cortex and its disorders. He is an author of the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, where he has notably contributed a chapter focused on the adrenal cortex. Through his research and writings, Stewart PM has established himself as a significant figure in the study of adrenal health and related conditions."}{"title": "NEWELL-PRICE JDC:Newell-Price JDC is a distinguished medical professional and researcher known for their contributions to the field of endocrinology. They co-authored the chapter on the adrenal cortex in the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, showcasing their expertise and involvement in academic literature. Additionally, Newell-Price JDC has made significant contributions to the study of the adrenal cortex, further establishing their reputation as an authority in this area of research."}{"title": "HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL (HTA):Hypertension Arterial (HTA) is a medical condition characterized by consistently high blood pressure, which can lead to various health complications. It may be associated with adrenal disorders and is often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas. This condition requires careful monitoring and management to prevent potential health risks associated with elevated blood pressure levels."}{"title": "HYPERTENSION RESISTANT:Resistant hypertension refers to high blood pressure that remains above target levels despite the use of multiple antihypertensive medications."}{"title": "PRIMARY ALDOSTERONISM:Primary aldosteronism is a medical condition characterized by excessive secretion of aldosterone, which is a common cause of secondary hypertension. This condition results in elevated blood pressure and can lead to electrolyte imbalances."}{"title": "M\u00c9XICO DF:Mexico City (DF) is the capital of Mexico, known for being a significant hub for medical publications and guidelines. It is notable for the publication of the Spanish edition of Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, which underscores its importance in the medical field."}{"title": "HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL:Hypertension arterial (HTA) is a specific type of hypertension that affects the arteries, resulting in an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases. It is recognized as a significant risk factor associated with diabetes, further elevating the likelihood of developing cardiovascular complications."}{"title": "ALDOSTERONE:Aldosterone is a steroid hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium and potassium levels in the blood. This regulation is significant as it influences blood pressure. The secretion of aldosterone is suppressed when there are high levels of deoxycorticosterone acetate (DOCA) present in the body."}{"title": "HYPERTENSION RESISTENTE:Resistant hypertension refers to high blood pressure that remains above target levels despite the use of multiple antihypertensive medications."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE APNEA-HIPOXIA DEL SUE\u00d1O:Sleep apnea-hypopnea syndrome is a disorder characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep, which can contribute to hypertension."}{"title": "DIAGN\u00d3STICO DE HIPOALDOSTERONISMO:Diagnosis of hypoaldosteronism involves identifying insufficient aldosterone production, which can lead to electrolyte imbalances and low blood pressure."}{"title": "HIPOALDOSTERONISMO:Hipoaldosteronismo is a medical condition characterized by the insufficient production of aldosterone, a hormone crucial for regulating sodium and potassium levels in the body. This deficiency can lead to significant imbalances in these electrolytes, often resulting in conditions such as hyponatremia (low sodium levels) and hyperkalemia (high potassium levels). The condition affects the body's ability to maintain proper electrolyte balance, which is essential for various physiological functions."}{"title": "HIPOALDOSTERONISMO HIPORRENIN\u00c9MICO:Hyporeninemic hypoaldosteronism is a specific type of hypoaldosteronism where there is low renin activity alongside low aldosterone levels."}{"title": "HIPOALDOSTERONISMO SECUNDARIO:HIPOALDOSTERONISMO SECUNDARIO, or secondary hypoaldosteronism, is a condition characterized by reduced production of aldosterone due to factors that originate outside the adrenal glands. This condition arises from external influences that disrupt the normal functioning of the adrenal glands, leading to decreased aldosterone levels. Common causes include adrenal gland damage and various hormonal imbalances that interfere with the regulation of aldosterone production."}{"title": "HIPOALDOSTERONISMO PRIMARIO:Primary hypoaldosteronism is a condition where the adrenal glands fail to produce sufficient aldosterone, often leading to electrolyte imbalances."}{"title": "BORNSTEIN SR:Bornstein SR is an author recognized for contributing to the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline concerning the diagnosis and treatment of primary adrenal insufficiency. This work has been published in the Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism, where Bornstein SR provided essential guidelines aimed at improving the understanding and management of this condition."}{"title": "ALLOLIO B:Allolio B is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline on the diagnosis and treatment of primary adrenal insufficiency."}{"title": "ARLT W:Arlt W is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline on the diagnosis and treatment of primary adrenal insufficiency."}{"title": "YOUNG WF:Young WF is an author associated with UpToDate, where he provides literature reviews on adrenal incidentalomas. In addition to this, he has written extensively on the diagnosis of primary aldosteronism and endocrine hypertension. His contributions to the field highlight his expertise in endocrinology, particularly in the areas related to adrenal disorders and hypertension."}{"title": "HIPOPOTASEMIA:HIPOPOTASEMIA, also known as hypokalemia, is a medical condition characterized by low levels of potassium in the blood. This electrolyte disturbance can significantly affect muscle function and heart rhythm, leading to symptoms such as muscle weakness and potential cardiac issues. It is particularly common in patients receiving enteral nutrition, where low potassium levels can result in various health complications. Management of hipopotasemia may involve dietary adjustments, specifically a high potassium diet, in certain medical situations. Overall, hipopotasemia is often associated with nutritional deficiencies and requires careful monitoring and treatment to prevent serious health risks."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISMO:Hiperaldosteronismo es un trastorno endocrino en el que hay una producci\u00f3n excesiva de aldosterona, lo que puede resultar en hipertensi\u00f3n y desequilibrios electrol\u00edticos."}{"title": "ESPIRONOLACTONA:Espironolactona, also known as spironolactone, is a potassium-sparing diuretic that plays a crucial role in managing various medical conditions. It is primarily used to help the body eliminate excess fluid, making it effective in treating heart failure and hypertension. Additionally, espironolactona is utilized in the management of hyperaldosteronism, a condition characterized by excessive production of the hormone aldosterone.\n\nBeyond its diuretic properties, spironolactone functions as an aldosterone antagonist, which means it blocks the effects of aldosterone, a hormone that can lead to fluid retention and increased blood pressure. This mechanism is particularly important when assessing the aldosterone/renin plasma activity ratio, as the medication must be withdrawn prior to testing to ensure accurate results.\n\nMoreover, spironolactone has applications in hormone therapy, particularly for transgender women, as it blocks androgen receptors, contributing to the desired hormonal effects in this population. Overall, espironolactona is a versatile medication with significant implications in both cardiovascular health and hormone therapy."}{"title": "YOUNG WF, JR.:Young WF, Jr. is a distinguished medical expert recognized for his significant contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the diagnosis and management of primary aldosteronism and endocrine hypertension. He has authored numerous works that enhance the understanding of these conditions. Additionally, Young WF, Jr. has made substantial contributions to the literature regarding pheochromocytoma, focusing on its clinical presentation, diagnosis, and treatment. His expertise is reflected in his involvement in various medical guidelines and publications, establishing him as a prominent figure in the medical community."}{"title": "CORTEX SUPRARRENAL:The adrenal cortex is the outer region of the adrenal glands, responsible for producing hormones such as aldosterone."}{"title": "11-DESOXICORTICOSTERONA:11-Deoxycorticosterone is a steroid hormone that can influence blood pressure and electrolyte balance, often associated with conditions affecting aldosterone levels."}{"title": "DOCA:DOCA, or Deoxycorticosterone, is a steroid hormone that plays a significant role in the regulation of blood pressure and electrolyte balance. When present in excess, DOCA can lead to conditions such as hypertension and hypokalemia. Additionally, Deoxycorticosterone acetate (DOCA) is a synthetic form of this mineralocorticoid, which is known to cause hypertension and is associated with the secretion of aldosterone. Overall, both forms of DOCA are linked to increased blood pressure and electrolyte imbalances, highlighting their importance in endocrine and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "HIPERALDOSTERONISMO PRIMARIO:Hiperaldosteronismo primario, tambi\u00e9n conocido como primary hyperaldosteronism, es un trastorno endocrino caracterizado por la producci\u00f3n excesiva de aldosterona. Esta condici\u00f3n puede resultar en hipertensi\u00f3n y hipokalemia, as\u00ed como en otros problemas de salud. Adem\u00e1s, el hiperaldosteronismo primario es un \u00e1rea de investigaci\u00f3n importante para Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez, quien se enfoca en los trastornos endocrinos relacionados con esta condici\u00f3n."}{"title": "CYP11B2:CYP11B2 is a gene that plays a crucial role in the production of aldosterone, a hormone that regulates sodium and potassium levels in the body. Its genetic variations are significant in the context of familial hyperaldosteronism type 1, a condition characterized by excessive production of aldosterone."}{"title": "CYP11B:CYP11B refers to the gene coding for 11-\u03b2-hydroxylase, which is involved in steroid hormone biosynthesis."}{"title": "CYP17:CYP17 refers to the gene coding for 17-\u03b1-hydroxylase, which plays a role in the production of steroid hormones."}{"title": "HYPOKALEMIA:Hypokalemia is a medical condition characterized by low potassium levels in the blood. This condition can significantly impact various populations, including preterm infants, who may be particularly vulnerable to its effects. Additionally, hypokalemia is often associated with excess levels of deoxycorticosterone acetate (DOCA), which can contribute to the development of this electrolyte imbalance."}{"title": "GEN QUIM\u00c9RICO:A chimeric gene resulting from the crossover of sequences between CYP11B1 and CYP11B2, affecting aldosterone production."}{"title": "HISTORIA FAMILIAR:The term \"HISTORIA FAMILIAR\" refers to the medical history of family members, which can play a crucial role in understanding various health conditions and their genetic predispositions. Family history is particularly significant in diagnosing primary hyperaldosteronism, especially among young patients presenting with hypertension. Additionally, it can indicate a genetic predisposition to conditions such as nephrolithiasis. Furthermore, a family history of type 1 diabetes, growth retardation, iron deficiency anemia, and steatorrhea may serve as risk factors for celiac disease. Moreover, the history of atopic diseases within a family can influence the likelihood of developing food allergies. Overall, \"HISTORIA FAMILIAR\" encompasses a wide range of hereditary health issues that can impact individual health outcomes."}{"title": "RESISTENCIA PRIMARIA AL CORTISOL:Primary cortisol resistance is a rare familial syndrome characterized by increased cortisol secretion without clinical signs of hypercortisolism."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME FAMILIAR:A hereditary syndrome that can lead to primary hyperaldosteronism, often presenting with hypertension and a family history of similar conditions."}{"title": "HISTORIA FAMILIAR DE HIPERTENSI\u00d3N:Family history of hypertension can indicate a genetic predisposition to conditions like primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "PRUEBAS CL\u00c1SICAS INDIRECTAS:Classic indirect tests, such as the dexamethasone suppression test, are used for diagnosing conditions like primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "ESTUDIO GEN\u00c9TICO DIRECTO:Direct genetic testing is recommended for diagnosing familial hyperaldosteronism and should replace classic indirect tests."}{"title": "ICTUS A UNA EDAD JOVEN:Stroke at a young age can be associated with familial hyperaldosteronism and may indicate a genetic risk factor."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N RESISTENTE:Resistant hypertension is a condition where blood pressure remains high despite treatment, often linked to primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "TUMORES SUPRARRENALES:"}{"title": "HIPERALDOSTERONISMO FAMILIAR TIPO 2:El hiperaldosteronismo familiar de tipo 2 es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico dominante que no presenta supresi\u00f3n de aldosterona con dexametasona y se relaciona con la regi\u00f3n 7p22."}{"title": "CYP11B1:El gen CYP11B1 tambi\u00e9n est\u00e1 relacionado con la producci\u00f3n de hormonas esteroides y su intercambio con CYP11B2 es significativo en el hiperaldosteronismo familiar tipo 1."}{"title": "ADENOMA PRODUCTOR DE ALDOSTERONA:Aldosterone-producing adenoma is a type of tumor in the adrenal gland that secretes excess aldosterone, causing primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "ADRENALCTOMY:Adrenalectomy is a surgical procedure to remove one or both adrenal glands, often performed to treat conditions like hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "RENIN:Renin is an enzyme secreted by the kidneys that plays a crucial role in blood pressure regulation and fluid balance."}{"title": "MANEJO DE HIPERALDOSTERONISMO:Management of hyperaldosteronism involves diagnosis, treatment options including surgery, and monitoring of aldosterone and renin levels."}{"title": "NIVEL DE RENINA:Renin levels are measured to assess the activity of the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system, which is crucial in diagnosing conditions like hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN SODIO:A sodium-rich diet may be recommended to prevent hyperkalemia in patients with hypoaldosteronism following adrenal surgery."}{"title": "METANEFRINAS:METANEFRINAS are biochemical markers utilized in the diagnosis of adrenal tumors and related conditions, particularly pheochromocytoma and paragangliomas. They are metabolites of catecholamines, which are substances produced by the adrenal glands. These metabolites are typically measured in urine tests, serving as a diagnostic marker for pheochromocytoma, a type of tumor that can affect adrenal function. Additionally, metanephrines are assessed in laboratory tests to evaluate patients with adrenal incidentalomas, helping to identify potential underlying tumors. Overall, the measurement of metanephrines plays a crucial role in the diagnostic process for various adrenal-related conditions."}{"title": "YODO-COLESTEROL:A treatment option for malignant pheochromocytoma involving the administration of radioactive iodine-labeled cholesterol."}{"title": "FENOXIBENZAMIDA:Fenoxibenzamida is a medication specifically utilized for the preoperative management of pheochromocytoma, a type of tumor that can cause hypertensive crises. It is recognized as the drug of choice for achieving alpha-blockade in this context, effectively helping to control blood pressure and mitigate the risks associated with surgery for patients suffering from this condition."}{"title": "TUMORES SECRETORES DE CATECOLAMINAS:Tumors that secrete catecholamines, including pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, affecting the body's stress response."}{"title": "CROMAFINES:Cells in the adrenal medulla and sympathetic ganglia that produce catecholamines and are involved in the development of pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "MUTACIONES EN L\u00cdNEA GERMINAL:Genetic mutations that can be identified in some cases of pheochromocytomas, contributing to familial forms of the disease."}{"title": "NEFROANGIOESCLEROSIS:"}{"title": "MIBG:MIBG (metaiodobenzylguanidine) is a radiopharmaceutical utilized in both the diagnosis and treatment of tumors that secrete catecholamines, with a particular focus on pheochromocytoma. It serves as an important tool in imaging, allowing for the detection of pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas. MIBG provides valuable anatomical and functional information about these tumors, enhancing the understanding and management of conditions associated with catecholamine-secreting tumors."}{"title": "D\u00cdAZ P\u00c9REZ JA:D\u00edaz P\u00e9rez JA is an author recognized for his contributions to the medical literature on pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas. He has specifically written about these topics in the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" highlighting his expertise in the field. His work is frequently referenced in discussions surrounding these endocrine tumors, underscoring his significance in advancing knowledge related to these conditions."}{"title": "CRESPO HERN\u00c1NDEZ I:Crespo Hern\u00e1ndez I is an author recognized for contributions to the medical literature concerning pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas. This individual has been referenced in various contexts related to these conditions, particularly noted for their work in the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" Through these contributions, Crespo Hern\u00e1ndez I has played a significant role in advancing the understanding of these endocrine tumors."}{"title": "CALCIOANTAGONISTAS:Calcioantagonistas are medications that can influence catecholamine levels, which may result in false positives in diagnostic tests for pheochromocytomas. Additionally, these medications can affect vascular resistance and may interfere with the diagnosis of pheochromocytoma, particularly when administered prior to MIBG testing."}{"title": "ANTIDEPRESIVOS TRIC\u00cdCLICOS:Antidepresivos tric\u00edclicos, or tricyclic antidepressants, are a class of medications known for their various effects on the body. They can interfere with the detection of catecholamines, which may result in false positives during testing. Additionally, these medications can inhibit gastric motility and affect the measurement of catecholamines and metanephrines in urine tests. Overall, antidepresivos tric\u00edclicos have significant implications for both diagnostic testing and gastrointestinal function."}{"title": "PARAGANGLIOMA:Paraganglioma is a rare tumor that arises from the paraganglia, which are neuroendocrine tissues associated with the autonomic nervous system. This type of tumor is often linked to genetic mutations and can occur in various locations throughout the body, although it is frequently found in the head and neck region. Paragangliomas are related to pheochromocytomas and can exhibit malignant behavior, with the potential to metastasize. Additionally, these tumors may produce catecholamines, further highlighting their connection to the nervous system and their association with certain genetic syndromes."}{"title": "SDHB:SDHB is a gene that plays a significant role in familial paraganglioma syndrome type 4, which is characterized by the development of paragangliomas and other tumors. It is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, particularly affecting the adrenal glands. Mutations in the SDHB gene can lead to an increased risk of tumor development, including the potential for metastatic disease in pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas. Overall, SDHB is crucial in understanding the genetic susceptibility to these types of tumors."}{"title": "CRISIS HIPERTENSIVAS:Crisis hipertensivas are episodes of high blood pressure that can occur in patients with feocromocitomas and require careful management."}{"title": "VON HIPPEL-LINDAU:Von Hippel-Lindau is an autosomal dominant disorder that affects approximately 1 in 35,000 people. It is characterized by the presence of various tumors, including pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, among others. This genetic condition leads to the development of multiple tumor types, highlighting its significant impact on affected individuals."}{"title": "SUCCINATE DEHYDROGENASE:Succinato deshidrogenasa (SDH) is a mitochondrial enzyme complex involved in the tricarboxylic acid cycle and is associated with tumor suppression."}{"title": "PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA:Pheochromocytoma is a tumor of the adrenal gland that produces catecholamines, leading to various clinical symptoms."}{"title": "VHL GENE:The VHL gene is a tumor suppressor gene associated with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome and is involved in the regulation of hypoxia-inducible factors."}{"title": "HARRISON'S PRINCIPLES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE:"}{"title": "JWM:JWM is a lender involved in the clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma."}{"title": "DUH QY:DUH QY is a lender mentioned in the context of pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma guidelines."}{"title": "EISENHOFER G:Eisenhofer G is a lender associated with the clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma."}{"title": "GIMENEZ-ROQUEPLO AP:Gimenez-Roqueplo AP is a lender involved in the clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma."}{"title": "GREBE SKG:Grebe SKG is a lender mentioned in the context of pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma guidelines."}{"title": "PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA AND PARAGANGLIOMA:Pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma are medical conditions addressed in the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guidelines."}{"title": "MET\u00c1STASIS:MET\u00c1STASIS refers to the process by which cancer cells spread from the original tumor site to other parts of the body. This phenomenon can involve various organs, including the liver, bones, and adrenal glands. Additionally, metastasis may be associated with the carcinoid syndrome, which is a group of symptoms that can occur in patients with certain types of cancer. Overall, MET\u00c1STASIS signifies a critical aspect of cancer progression, highlighting the ability of cancer cells to invade and affect multiple areas beyond their initial location."}{"title": "MIELOLIPOMA:Mielolipoma is a rare benign tumor of the adrenal gland composed of adipose tissue and hematopoietic elements."}{"title": "QUISTES:Quistes are fluid-filled sacs that can occur in the adrenal glands and may be discovered incidentally."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The European Society of Endocrinology is a professional organization dedicated to providing clinical practice guidelines for the management of endocrine disorders. This includes specific guidelines for the management of adrenal incidentalomas, which are incidental findings of adrenal tumors that may or may not be clinically significant. The organization plays a crucial role in standardizing care and improving outcomes for patients with various endocrine conditions, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest evidence-based practices in the field."}{"title": "CUSHING SYNDROME:A hormonal disorder caused by prolonged exposure to high levels of cortisol, which can be detected through various tests."}{"title": "FASSNACHT M:Fassnacht M is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. He is actively involved in the management guidelines for these conditions and participates in endocrinology research. Additionally, Fassnacht M is recognized as one of the authors of the article addressing the management of adrenal incidentalomas within the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines."}{"title": "BANCOS I:Bancos I is a significant contributor to the management guidelines for adrenal incidentalomas, emphasizing clinical practice in the field of endocrinology. Additionally, Bancos I is recognized as an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines specifically addressing the management of adrenal incidentalomas."}{"title": "NEWELL-PRICE J:Newell-Price J is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. This individual is recognized for their significant research in adrenal disorders and has played a key role in developing management guidelines for these conditions. As an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas, Newell-Price J has contributed valuable insights and expertise to the field."}{"title": "SAHDEV A:Sahdev A is a notable contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. He has played a significant role in the development of management guidelines for these conditions, demonstrating his involvement in the field of clinical endocrinology. As an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas, Sahdev A's expertise and contributions are integral to the understanding and treatment of this area in endocrinology."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE CUSHING SUBCL\u00cdNICO:El s\u00edndrome de Cushing subcl\u00ednico es un estado transitorio que puede revertir y que puede progresar a un s\u00edndrome de Cushing manifiesto, aunque su evoluci\u00f3n no est\u00e1 clara y es poco frecuente."}{"title": "HORMONAS SEXUALES:HORMONAS SEXUALES, or sex hormones, are crucial hormones that regulate the development and functioning of reproductive organs. This group includes hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone), LH (luteinizing hormone), and testosterone, as well as androgens and estrogens. The measurement of sex hormones is particularly important in clinical scenarios where there is a suspicion of adrenal carcinoma, as their secretion by a benign adenoma is quite rare. In cases of adrenal incidentalomas, where there is a clinical suspicion of malignancy, it is essential to evaluate the potential secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors. Thus, the assessment of these hormones plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of conditions related to the adrenal glands and reproductive health."}{"title": "YOUNG WF, JR:Young WF, Jr es el autor del art\u00edculo sobre el incidentaloma adrenal en UpToDate, que proporciona informaci\u00f3n actualizada sobre el tema."}{"title": "ALD/ARP:The aldosterone/renin plasma activity ratio is a test performed to assess adrenal function, particularly in cases of primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "EPLERENONA:Eplerenone is another aldosterone antagonist similar to spironolactone, which also requires withdrawal before testing for accurate interpretation."}{"title": "SECRECI\u00d3N DE HORMONAS SEXUALES:The secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors is rare, typically associated with malignant conditions."}{"title": "GUIAS:Guidelines refer to the recommendations for the management and follow-up of adrenal incidentalomas, which may vary based on initial imaging characteristics."}{"title": "ADRENAL INCIDENTALOMA:ADRENAL INCIDENTALOMA is a medical condition characterized by the discovery of an adrenal mass that is not associated with symptoms of adrenal dysfunction. This condition typically arises incidentally during imaging studies conducted for unrelated reasons, and it does not present any clinical symptoms related to adrenal hormone overproduction or deficiency."}{"title": "BANKOS I:Bankos I is a contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on adrenal incidentalomas."}{"title": "TAC ABDOMINAL:TAC abdominal, also known as a computed tomography (CT) scan of the abdomen, is a diagnostic imaging procedure utilized primarily to identify incidentalomas in the adrenal glands and to detect masses or abnormalities within the abdominal region. This imaging technique has been instrumental in confirming diagnoses, such as pancreatic adenocarcinoma, by providing detailed images that help in the assessment of various conditions affecting the abdominal organs."}{"title": "DHEA:Dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) is a weak androgen hormone produced by the adrenal glands. It plays a significant role in the body's hormonal balance and is often measured in the evaluation of adrenal function. DHEA can activate certain steroid receptors, albeit with lower affinity. In cases of aromatase deficiency, DHEA levels may be elevated, which can contribute to virilization symptoms. Additionally, DHEA is relevant in the study of adrenal incidentalomas, as it is an important marker in assessing adrenal health. It is noteworthy that DHEA can be converted into more potent androgens, such as testosterone, further emphasizing its role in the endocrine system."}{"title": "POTASSIUM:Potassium is an essential mineral and electrolyte that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is commonly measured in blood tests to assess adrenal function and other health conditions. Found abundantly in fruits, vegetables, and other foods, potassium is vital for heart health and may aid in controlling blood pressure, particularly in individuals with high sodium intake. \n\nIn addition to its cardiovascular benefits, potassium influences kidney health and the formation of kidney stones. It helps regulate fluid balance in the body, making it important for overall health. However, potassium intake may need to be restricted in the diets of certain patients, especially those with chronic kidney disease, to prevent complications such as hyperkalemia. For patients without diuresis undergoing treatment with ACE inhibitors, potassium intake should not exceed 1 mEq/kg/day. Consequently, potassium levels are closely monitored and managed in dietary recommendations for individuals with kidney issues to ensure their health and well-being."}{"title": "GLUCOSE:GLUCOSE is a simple sugar that serves as a primary energy source for the body and is critical for cellular function. It is often measured in blood tests for metabolic assessment and plays a significant role in diabetes management. As a non-essential nutrient, glucose can be obtained through various metabolic pathways, making it vital for energy, especially in critically ill patients. Additionally, glucose is important in the context of PET scans, where it is utilized to assess metabolic activity. In dietary management, glucose may be administered intravenously to patients undergoing surgical procedures related to metabolic disorders. Overall, glucose is a key component of many carbohydrates and is essential for the energy needs of living organisms."}{"title": "PANCREATITIS LITI\u00c1SICA:A medical condition that led to the admission of the patient, which is characterized by inflammation of the pancreas due to gallstones."}{"title": "HORMONAL STUDIES:Tests conducted to evaluate adrenal function and assess the presence of conditions like Cushing's syndrome or hyperaldosteronism in patients with incidentalomas."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISM PRIMARIO:A condition that may be screened for in patients with adrenal incidentalomas, characterized by excessive production of aldosterone."}{"title": "HYPERALDOSTERONISMO PRIMARIO:A condition characterized by excessive production of aldosterone, often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas."}{"title": "DIUR\u00c9TICOS:Diur\u00e9ticos, or diuretics, are medications that promote the excretion of water and salts from the body through urine. They are commonly used in the treatment of conditions such as hypertension and edema, as they help to alleviate fluid retention. Diuretics can significantly affect sodium levels and are relevant in the context of diagnosing conditions like SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion). Additionally, they may influence the evaluation of adrenal function in patients with adrenal incidentalomas and can impact electrolyte balance, particularly in individuals with adrenal insufficiency.\n\nThese medications can also affect magnesium reabsorption in the kidneys, potentially leading to changes in magnesium levels and causing conditions such as hypomagnesemia or hypermagnesiuria. Furthermore, diuretics are known to promote the loss of potassium, which is an important consideration in their use. Overall, diur\u00e9ticos play a crucial role in managing fluid balance and electrolyte levels in various medical conditions."}{"title": "ANTAGONISTAS DE LA ALDOSTERONA:A class of medications that block the effects of aldosterone, relevant in the context of hyperaldosteronism and adrenal incidentalomas."}{"title": "HORMONAS ADRENALINA:Hormones produced by the adrenal glands that are involved in the body's stress response, relevant in the context of adrenal tumors."}{"title": "ADENOMA BENIGNO:A benign tumor of the adrenal gland that rarely secretes sex hormones."}{"title": "HIDROXIPROGESTERONA:17-hidroxiprogesterona is a hormone that should be measured in cases of bilateral adrenal incidentalomas to rule out congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency."}{"title": "SUPRARRENAL:The term \"suprarrenal\" refers to the adrenal glands, which are located above the kidneys. These glands play a crucial role in the endocrine system, producing important hormones such as cortisol and adrenaline. In the context of medical conditions, suprarrenal glands are often discussed in relation to incidentalomas and disorders associated with them. Additionally, they are known to be the site where tumors such as feochromocitomas and paragangliomas can develop. Overall, the suprarrenal glands are vital components of the body's hormonal regulation and are involved in various health conditions."}{"title": "FAASSNACHT M:Fassnacht M is an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas."}{"title": "ADRENOCORTICAL CARCINOMA:Adrenocortical carcinoma is a rare cancer of the adrenal cortex, with an incidence of 1 in 1,000,000 people per year, often requiring surgical intervention for localized disease."}{"title": "STEWARD PM:Steward PM is an author referenced in the literature regarding the adrenal cortex and its disorders."}{"title": "HIPOGONADISMO:Hipogonadismo es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica caracterizada por concentraciones bajas de testosterona en sangre y un deterioro de la espermatog\u00e9nesis. Esta condici\u00f3n se manifiesta cuando el cuerpo no produce suficientes hormonas sexuales, lo que puede dar lugar a diversos problemas de salud, incluyendo la infertilidad. Adem\u00e1s, el hipogonadismo se asocia a menudo con una secreci\u00f3n reducida o ausente de hormonas desde las g\u00f3nadas. En algunos casos, el tratamiento con mitotano puede estar relacionado con esta condici\u00f3n. En resumen, el hipogonadismo implica una deficiencia en la producci\u00f3n de testosterona y puede tener m\u00faltiples repercusiones en la salud general del individuo."}{"title": "CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIO:Carcinoma suprarrenal primario is a rare cancer with an incidence of 1 in 1,000,000 inhabitants per year, more frequently affecting women than men."}{"title": "HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONGENITA:Congenital adrenal hyperplasia is a genetic disorder with autosomal recessive inheritance affecting cortisol synthesis enzymes."}{"title": "GLANDULA SUPRARRENAL:The adrenal gland is responsible for producing hormones such as cortisol and aldosterone, and is involved in the body's response to stress."}{"title": "21-HIDROXILASA:La 21-hidroxilasa es una enzima cuya deficiencia causa hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita, afectando la producci\u00f3n de hormonas esteroides."}{"title": "ARLT W.:ARLT W. es un autor que ha escrito sobre trastornos de la corteza suprarrenal, incluyendo la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita."}{"title": "TREATMENT OF CLASSIC CONGENITAL ADRENAL HYPERPLASIA:"}{"title": "CROMOSOMA 6:El cromosoma 6 es el cromosoma humano donde se localiza el gen CYP21A2, relacionado con la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita."}{"title": "KASPER DL.:Kasper DL. es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura m\u00e9dica sobre medicina interna, incluyendo temas relacionados con la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita."}{"title": "SPEISER PW.:Speiser PW. es un autor que ha escrito gu\u00edas de pr\u00e1ctica sobre la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita debido a la deficiencia de 21-hidroxilasa."}{"title": "TETRACOSACTIDA:La tetracosactida es un medicamento utilizado en pruebas de estimulaci\u00f3n con ACTH para evaluar la funci\u00f3n adrenal en pacientes con sospecha de hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita."}{"title": "GENOTIPO-FENOTIPO:El genotipo-fenotipo en la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita se refiere a la relaci\u00f3n entre las mutaciones gen\u00e9ticas y las manifestaciones cl\u00ednicas de la enfermedad."}{"title": "HETEROCIGOTOS:Los heterocigotos compuestos para las mutaciones pat\u00f3genas en el gen CYP21A2 son comunes en pacientes con hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AGUDA:Acute adrenal insufficiency is a medical emergency characterized by low blood pressure and volume depletion, requiring immediate treatment."}{"title": "SUERO FISIOLOGICO:Saline solution is used in the treatment of patients in shock due to acute adrenal insufficiency to restore fluid balance."}{"title": "UVI MOVIL:Mobile Intensive Care Unit (UVI Movil) is a medical unit that provides emergency care and transport for critically ill patients."}{"title": "ELSEVIER:Elsevier is a global information analytics business that specializes in scientific, technical, and medical content. It is recognized for its extensive portfolio in scientific publishing, which includes a variety of medical textbooks and journals. Among its notable publications is the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology. While some of its operations are based in Madrid, Elsevier's influence and reach extend worldwide, making it a prominent entity in the field of medical and scientific literature."}{"title": "TUMOR PRODUCTOR DE CATECOLAMINAS:Tumors that produce catecholamines can lead to various clinical symptoms and are significant in the context of adrenal disorders."}{"title": "GEN RET:The RET gene is associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia and is significant in the context of genetic testing for patients with feochromocytomas."}{"title": "GEN VHL:GEN VHL refers to the VHL gene, which is a crucial tumor suppressor gene. When mutated, it is associated with various neoplasms, including feocromocitoma. The VHL gene is also linked to von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, a genetic condition that can lead to the development of multiple tumors. This gene plays a significant role in the genetic assessment of patients with adrenal tumors, highlighting its importance in both cancer predisposition and clinical evaluation."}{"title": "GEN SDHB:The SDHB gene is involved in the development of certain tumors, including paragangliomas and is relevant for genetic testing in affected patients."}{"title": "GEN SDHC:The SDHC gene is associated with hereditary paraganglioma and is important for genetic counseling in families with a history of these tumors."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE VON HIPPEL-LINDAU:Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome is a genetic disorder characterized by an increased risk of developing various tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors and pheochromocytomas. This condition is inherited in an autosomal dominant manner, meaning that it can be passed down from one generation to the next. Individuals with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome may experience a range of tumor types due to the genetic mutations associated with the disorder."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA ENDOCRINA M\u00daLTIPLE TIPO 2:Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 2 (MEN 2) is a genetic syndrome characterized by a hereditary predisposition to the development of tumors in endocrine glands. This condition significantly increases the risk of developing various endocrine tumors, including feocromocitomas, which are tumors of the adrenal glands. MEN 2 encompasses a range of endocrine neoplasms, highlighting the importance of genetic screening and monitoring for individuals affected by this syndrome."}{"title": "NEUROFIBROMATOSIS DE TIPO 1:Neurofibromatosis type 1 is a genetic disorder that can be associated with feocromocitomas, although less commonly than the other syndromes mentioned."}{"title": "SDHC:SDHC is a gene that is associated with the development of hereditary pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, which are types of tumors that arise from adrenal gland tissue and nerve tissue, respectively. This gene plays a significant role in the cellular response to hypoxia, which is a condition characterized by insufficient oxygen levels. Additionally, SDHC is involved in mitochondrial function, indicating its importance in energy production and cellular metabolism. Overall, SDHC is crucial in the pathogenesis of these tumors and in maintaining normal cellular functions under varying oxygen conditions."}{"title": "VHL:The VHL gene, located on chromosome 3p25-26, encodes a protein that plays a crucial role in regulating hypoxia-induced proteins. Mutations in the VHL gene are associated with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, a genetic condition that significantly increases the risk of developing pheochromocytomas, as well as other tumors. This syndrome highlights the importance of the VHL gene in tumorigenesis and its role in the body's response to low oxygen levels."}{"title": "SDHD:SDHD is a gene that is significant in the development of paragangliomas and pheochromocytomas, particularly in the context of hypoxia. It is one of the key genes associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, and it plays a crucial role in mitochondrial function."}{"title": "PARAGANGLIOMAS:Paragangliomas are tumors that can occur alongside feocromocitomas and are associated with the secretion of catecholamines, affecting patients with certain genetic syndromes."}{"title": "GENES DE SUSCEPTIBILIDAD:Genes of susceptibility are genetic factors that increase the risk of developing feocromocitomas and paragangliomas, including SDHB, SDHC, and others."}{"title": "ANATOMOPATOL\u00d3GICO:Anatomopathological report refers to the examination of tissues to diagnose diseases, including tumors like feocromocitomas."}{"title": "GEN\u00c9TICO:Genetic study refers to the analysis of genes to identify mutations associated with feocromocitomas and paragangliomas."}{"title": "NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TIPO 1:Neurofibromatosis Type 1 is a genetic disorder that can also be associated with feocromocitomas, although less frequently than other syndromes."}{"title": "ATOVASTATINA:Atorvastatin is a medication that can cause false positives in the measurement of catecholamines and metanephrines."}{"title": "ANFETAMINAS:ANFETAMINAS, also known as amphetamines, are a class of stimulant drugs that can elevate catecholamine levels in the body. This elevation can lead to false positives in laboratory tests, particularly in the assessment of catecholamines in patients suspected of having pheochromocytomas. The elimination of anfetaminas can be enhanced through dietary acidification. Historically, anfetaminas were utilized starting in 1936 for weight loss purposes; however, their use was discontinued due to concerns over dependence, abuse, and potential cardiovascular effects."}{"title": "COCA\u00cdNA:Cocaine, known as \"coca\u00edna\" in Spanish, is a drug that can cause elevated levels of catecholamines and metanephrines in the body. This elevation can result in false positives during medical tests, particularly complicating the diagnosis of pheochromocytomas, which are tumors that can affect catecholamine levels. The presence of cocaine in the system can therefore interfere with accurate medical assessments and diagnoses."}{"title": "SUPRARRENALCTOM\u00cdA BILATERAL:Bilateral adrenalectomy is a surgical procedure performed to remove both adrenal glands, often due to the presence of feocromocitomas."}{"title": "HALLAZGO:Findings refer to the results obtained from imaging studies or tests that indicate the presence of feocromocitomas or paragangliomas."}{"title": "RET:RET is a proto-oncogene that plays a significant role in multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2). Mutations in the RET gene are linked to various endocrine disorders, particularly MEN2A and MEN2B, which increase the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and pheochromocytoma. The gene's involvement in these conditions highlights its importance in endocrine tumorigenesis, making it a critical focus for understanding and managing these syndromes."}{"title": "NF1:The NF1 gene is associated with neurofibromatosis type 1 and can lead to the development of pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "MAX:The MAX gene is involved in the regulation of cell growth and is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "TMEM127:The TMEM127 gene is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas and is involved in cellular signaling."}{"title": "TAC CON CONTRASTE:TAC con contraste is a specific imaging test used to detect tumors, particularly pheochromocytomas, due to its high spatial resolution."}{"title": "GAMMAGRAF\u00cdA:Gammagraf\u00eda is a functional imaging test used to detect pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, providing information about tumor activity."}{"title": "FLUORODESOXIGLUCOSA:Fluorodesoxiglucosa is a radiotracer used in PET scans, considered more sensitive for detecting metastases of malignant paragangliomas compared to MIBG."}{"title": "LABETALOL:Labetalol is a medication that can interfere with catecholamine testing, leading to false positives in patients suspected of having pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "HISTOQU\u00cdMICA:Inmunohistoqu\u00edmica is a technique used to analyze tissue samples for the presence of specific proteins, which can help identify mutations in genes related to pheochromocytomas."}{"title": "ESPECIFICIDAD:Especificidad refers to the ability of a test to correctly identify patients without pheochromocytomas, which is crucial for accurate diagnosis.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MART\u00cdN L\u00d3PEZ DE LA TORRE CASARES:Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, with a Doctorate in Medicine from the University of Bologna and currently serves as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at the Hospital Universitario Virgen de las Nieves in Granada."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE BOLONIA:The University of Bologna is where Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares obtained his Doctorate in Medicine in 1990."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD INTERNACIONAL MEN\u00c9NDEZ PELAYO:The Universidad Internacional Men\u00e9ndez Pelayo is where Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares completed his Master's in Clinical Management of Endocrinology and Nutrition in 2018."}{"title": "PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL:Central precocious puberty, known in Spanish as \"pubertad precoz central,\" is a condition characterized by the early activation of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis. This condition leads to the development of secondary sexual characteristics before the age of 8 in girls and before the age of 9 in boys. The early onset of puberty in this manner signifies a significant deviation from the typical developmental timeline, prompting further medical evaluation and potential intervention."}{"title": "STYNE DM:Styne DM es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la fisiolog\u00eda y los trastornos de la pubertad."}{"title": "GRUMBACH MM:Grumbach MM es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la fisiolog\u00eda y los trastornos de la pubertad."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LOGOS DE LA GNRH:Los an\u00e1logos de la GnRH son tratamientos utilizados para estabilizar la progresi\u00f3n puberal en casos de pubertad precoz central."}{"title": "EJE HIPOT\u00c1LAMO-HIP\u00d3FISO-GONADAL:El eje hipot\u00e1lamo-hip\u00f3fiso-gonadal es un sistema hormonal que regula la funci\u00f3n reproductiva y se activa durante la pubertad."}{"title": "EDAD \u00d3SEA:La edad \u00f3sea es un indicador del desarrollo f\u00edsico de un ni\u00f1o y se utiliza para evaluar la pubertad precoz al compararla con la edad cronol\u00f3gica."}{"title": "TRIPTORELINA:Triptorelina, also known as triptorelin, is a synthetic analog of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH). It is primarily utilized in the treatment of central precocious puberty, a condition characterized by the early onset of puberty. In addition to its use in managing this specific condition, triptorelina is also employed in various medical treatments related to hormone-related disorders."}{"title": "LEURPORELINA:LEURPORELINA is an analog of Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH) that is primarily utilized in the treatment of central precocious puberty. It is known for its effectiveness in managing hormone-sensitive conditions, similar to another synthetic analog of GnRH, leuprolide. Both compounds serve important roles in regulating hormonal activity and are used in various medical treatments related to hormonal imbalances."}{"title": "GONADOTROFINAS:GONADOTROFINAS son hormonas que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n del sistema reproductivo. Estas hormonas, que incluyen la LH (hormona luteinizante) y la FSH (hormona foliculoestimulante), estimulan las g\u00f3nadas y son fundamentales para la producci\u00f3n de testosterona y esperma. En pacientes con insuficiencia gonadal, como aquellos que padecen el s\u00edndrome de Turner, los niveles de gonadotrofinas tienden a aumentar, lo que indica su importancia en la funci\u00f3n reproductiva y el desarrollo sexual."}{"title": "LUFORAN:Luforan is a medication used in tests to assess the function of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis."}{"title": "TANNER:Tanner stages are a scale of physical development in children, adolescents, and adults, used to assess sexual maturity."}{"title": "PUBERTAD PRECOZ PERIF\u00c9RICA:Peripheral precocious puberty is a type of precocious puberty that occurs independently of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis."}{"title": "GONADOTROPINAS:GONADOTROPINAS son hormonas que pueden ser administradas en el tratamiento del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, con el objetivo de estimular la producci\u00f3n de testosterona."}{"title": "TESTOTOCICOSIS:La testotoxicosis es una condici\u00f3n que causa la maduraci\u00f3n precoz de las c\u00e9lulas de Leydig, resultando en un aumento de testosterona y desarrollo sexual temprano en varones."}{"title": "MCUNE-ALBRIGHT:El s\u00edndrome de McCune-Albright es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que se asocia con pubertad precoz, displasia fibrosa y manchas caf\u00e9 con leche en la piel."}{"title": "CELULAS DE LEYDIG:Las c\u00e9lulas de Leydig son c\u00e9lulas en los test\u00edculos que producen testosterona, y su maduraci\u00f3n puede ser prematura en casos de testotoxicosis."}{"title": "TIO MATERNO:El t\u00edo materno del paciente es mencionado como alguien que tambi\u00e9n experiment\u00f3 pubertad precoz, sugiriendo un posible patr\u00f3n hereditario en la familia."}{"title": "NIVELES DE TESTOSTERONA:Los niveles de testosterona son cruciales para determinar el desarrollo sexual en varones y se miden para diagnosticar condiciones como la pubertad precoz."}{"title": "ECOGRAF\u00cdA TESTICULAR:La ecograf\u00eda testicular es un procedimiento diagn\u00f3stico utilizado para evaluar el tama\u00f1o y la salud de los test\u00edculos en el contexto de la pubertad precoz."}{"title": "TAC DE SUPRARRENALES:La tomograf\u00eda axial computarizada (TAC) de suprarrenales es un estudio que se realiza para descartar patolog\u00edas tumorales en pacientes con pubertad precoz."}{"title": "RNM CEREBRAL:RNM CEREBRAL, or resonancia magn\u00e9tica cerebral, is a medical imaging procedure utilized to assess the brain and identify abnormalities. This imaging technique is particularly effective in detecting conditions such as the absence of the olfactory bulb, which is associated with Kallman syndrome. Additionally, RNM CEREBRAL serves as an examination to evaluate potential neurological causes of precocious puberty. Through its advanced imaging capabilities, RNM CEREBRAL plays a crucial role in diagnosing various neurological conditions."}{"title": "ANDROSTENDIONA:Androstendiona is a steroid hormone that is less potent than some of its counterparts but has the ability to activate steroid receptors. It can be elevated in cases of precocious puberty and is measured to assess hormonal function."}{"title": "17-OH-PROGESTERONA:17-OH-Progesterona is a hormone that plays a crucial role in assessing adrenal function. It is particularly relevant in diagnosing conditions associated with sexual differentiation and puberty. Additionally, 17-OH-Progesterona is measured to evaluate hormonal disorders in children experiencing precocious puberty. This hormone's levels can provide important insights into various endocrine disorders and developmental issues."}{"title": "MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT SYNDROME:McCune-Albright syndrome is a condition characterized by fibrous dysplasia, caf\u00e9-au-lait spots on the skin, and/or precocious puberty, affecting mostly females before the age of 2."}{"title": "ADRENARQUIA:Adrenarche is the period of maturation of the adrenal glands that leads to the production of androgens, which can cause early sexual development."}{"title": "HYPERANDROGENISM:Hyperandrogenism is a medical condition characterized by excessive levels of androgens in the body, particularly in females. This condition is often associated with disorders such as Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS). The elevated androgen levels can lead to a variety of symptoms, including hirsutism (excessive hair growth), irregular menstrual cycles, and virilization (development of male physical characteristics). Overall, hyperandrogenism manifests through various clinical symptoms that can significantly impact the health and well-being of affected individuals."}{"title": "CLITOROMEGALY:Clitoromegaly is an abnormal enlargement of the clitoris, often associated with elevated androgen levels."}{"title": "HYPOTHALAMIC PULSE GENERATOR:The hypothalamic pulse generator is a mechanism in the hypothalamus that regulates the release of GnRH in a pulsatile manner, influencing puberty onset."}{"title": "FEMALE PATIENT:A 15-year-old female patient referred for consultation due to delayed onset of puberty, with a family history of early puberty."}{"title": "PRECOCIOUS PUBERTY:Precocious puberty is the onset of secondary sexual characteristics before the typical age, often seen in females with McCune-Albright syndrome."}{"title": "FEMALE:Refers to individuals of the female sex, particularly in the context of the discussed conditions affecting puberty."}{"title": "MALE:Refers to individuals of the male sex, particularly in the context of the discussed conditions affecting puberty."}{"title": "FIBROUS DYSPLASIA:"}{"title": "CROWLEY WF, JR:Crowley WF, Jr is a medical professional who contributed to the literature on the approach to patients with delayed puberty."}{"title": "TROTAN GE:Trotman GE is a medical professional who has written about delayed puberty in female patients."}{"title": "AMENORREA PRIMARIA:Primary amenorrhea is the medical term for the absence of menstruation in a girl by age 15, which can be caused by various conditions affecting the gonadal axis."}{"title": "HAMARTOMA HIPOTAL\u00c1MICO:Hypothalamic hamartoma is a benign tumor that can affect hormonal regulation and may be related to primary amenorrhea."}{"title": "ESTRADIOL:Estradiol is a form of estrogen that plays a crucial role in the regulation of the female reproductive system. It is essential for the development of female secondary sexual characteristics and is commonly measured to evaluate the onset of puberty. In individuals with aromatase deficiency, estradiol levels are typically low, which can lead to various developmental issues. Overall, estradiol is a vital hormone in female health and development."}{"title": "HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO:HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO, or hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of sex hormones resulting from inadequate stimulation by the pituitary gland. This condition can be either congenital or acquired and often leads to delayed puberty due to the low levels of sex hormones."}{"title": "RETRASO CONSTITUCIONAL:Constitutional delay is a temporary condition in which a child grows and develops more slowly than peers but eventually catches up, often affecting the timing of puberty."}{"title": "CARIOTIPO:Karyotype is a test that examines the number and structure of chromosomes, used to identify genetic abnormalities that may affect puberty."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE KALLMAN:El s\u00edndrome de Kallman es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que causa hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo y anosmia, resultando en retraso puberal y amenorrea primaria en varones y mujeres."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE KLINEFELTER:El s\u00edndrome de Klinefelter es una condici\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica que afecta a hombres, caracterizada por la presencia de un cromosoma X adicional. Esta anomal\u00eda cromos\u00f3mica puede resultar en hipogonadismo, que se manifiesta como una disminuci\u00f3n en la producci\u00f3n de hormonas sexuales, as\u00ed como en un retraso en el desarrollo puberal. Adem\u00e1s, el s\u00edndrome puede influir en el desarrollo f\u00edsico y cognitivo de los varones, generando diversos problemas de salud. En resumen, el s\u00edndrome de Klinefelter es una condici\u00f3n que impacta tanto el desarrollo f\u00edsico como el cognitivo en los hombres debido a la presencia de un cromosoma X extra."}{"title": "ANOSMIA:La anosmia es la p\u00e9rdida del sentido del olfato, que puede ser un s\u00edntoma asociado con el s\u00edndrome de Kallman."}{"title": "CRIPTORQUIDIA:Cryptorchidism, also known as \"criptorquidia\" in Spanish, is a medical condition characterized by the failure of one or both testicles to descend into the scrotum. This condition can have implications for hormonal and pubertal development in males."}{"title": "ORQUIDOPEXIA:ORQUIDOPEXIA, also known as orchidopexy, is a surgical procedure designed to correct cryptorchidism, a condition where one or both testicles fail to descend into the scrotum. The procedure involves placing the undescended testicle into the scrotum, allowing for proper positioning and function. This intervention is crucial for the health and development of the testicles, as it helps prevent potential complications associated with cryptorchidism."}{"title": "RETARDO PUBERAL:El retraso puberal es una condici\u00f3n en la que el desarrollo f\u00edsico y hormonal de un adolescente se retrasa en comparaci\u00f3n con sus pares."}{"title": "ANOMAL\u00cdAS M\u00dcLLERIANAS:Las anomal\u00edas m\u00fcllerianas son malformaciones cong\u00e9nitas del tracto reproductivo femenino que pueden resultar en amenorrea primaria."}{"title": "P\u00c9RDIDA DE PESO/ANOREXIA NERVIOSA:La p\u00e9rdida de peso significativa o la anorexia nerviosa pueden llevar a la amenorrea primaria debido a la alteraci\u00f3n del equilibrio hormonal."}{"title": "DISGENESIA GONADAL:"}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MAESTRE DE SAN JUAN-KALLMAN:El s\u00edndrome de Maestre de San Juan-Kallman es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que se caracteriza por hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo cong\u00e9nito asociado a defectos olfativos, como anosmia o hiposmia."}{"title": "RNM:RNM, or Resonancia Magn\u00e9tica, is an advanced imaging technique utilized to visualize internal structures of the body. This method is particularly valuable in diagnosing various medical conditions, including the Maestre de San Juan-Kallman syndrome. Additionally, RNM, which stands for Resonancia Magn\u00e9tica Nuclear, plays a crucial role in assessing a patient's condition, especially in the detection of metastasis. Through its detailed imaging capabilities, RNM aids healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient care and treatment options."}{"title": "INHIBINA B:La inhibina B es una prote\u00edna producida por las c\u00e9lulas de Sertoli en los test\u00edculos, que regula la producci\u00f3n de hormonas sexuales y se utiliza en el diagn\u00f3stico de hipogonadismo."}{"title": "HORMONA ANTIM\u00dcLLERIANA:La hormona antim\u00fclleriana es una hormona que se mide para evaluar la funci\u00f3n ov\u00e1rica y testicular, y puede ser un indicador en el diagn\u00f3stico de hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo."}{"title": "RETARDO CONSTITUCIONAL DEL CRECIMIENTO:El retraso constitucional del crecimiento es una condici\u00f3n en la que un ni\u00f1o presenta un crecimiento m\u00e1s lento de lo normal, pero eventualmente alcanza su altura esperada, a diferencia del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo."}{"title": "PALADAR HENDIDO:Paladar Hendido, also known as cleft palate, is a congenital condition characterized by a malformation in the structure of the palate. This condition can significantly impact feeding, often necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate intake. Additionally, it has been noted that paladar hendido may occur in patients with hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, indicating a potential association with this hormonal condition."}{"title": "SORDERA NEUROL\u00d3GICA:La sordera neurol\u00f3gica es una posible anomal\u00eda fenot\u00edpica asociada con el hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, que puede afectar la audici\u00f3n de los pacientes."}{"title": "KLINEFELTER SYNDROME:Klinefelter Syndrome is a genetic condition that affects males, characterized by the presence of an extra X chromosome. This chromosomal anomaly leads to a range of physical and reproductive abnormalities, including hypogonadism, which is a condition of reduced hormone production. Additionally, individuals with Klinefelter Syndrome may experience cognitive challenges and have an increased risk of certain health issues, including specific types of cancer. It is recognized as the most common chromosomal sexual pathology in males, highlighting its significance in genetic and medical contexts."}{"title": "BOEHM U:Boehm U is one of the authors referenced in the European Consensus Statement on congenital hypogonadotropic hypogonadism."}{"title": "CROWLEY WF:Crowley WF is referenced in the context of approaches to patients with delayed puberty."}{"title": "ADDISON'S DISEASE:Addison's disease is an autoimmune disorder that is frequently seen in patients with Klinefelter syndrome."}{"title": "TROMBOEMBOLISM:Tromboembolism is a risk associated with Klinefelter syndrome due to thrombophilia."}{"title": "CANCER OF THE PROSTATE:Cancer of the prostate is a condition that individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at increased risk for compared to the general male population."}{"title": "BRONCHITIS CHRONIC:Chronic bronchitis is a pulmonary disease that individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at higher risk of developing."}{"title": "BRONCHIECTASIS:Bronchiectasis is a condition characterized by the permanent enlargement of parts of the airways in the lungs. This condition often results from infections or other factors that damage the airways. It is particularly relevant in patients with cystic fibrosis, as they may experience significant respiratory health issues due to this condition. Additionally, individuals with Klinefelter syndrome may also be predisposed to developing bronchiectasis, highlighting its association with various underlying health conditions."}{"title": "METABOLIC SYNDROME:Metabolic syndrome is a cluster of conditions that significantly increase the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes. This syndrome is often associated with various factors, including dietary habits, obesity, and insulin resistance. It is particularly prevalent in certain populations, such as patients with Klinefelter syndrome and individuals who have undergone liver transplantation. Management of metabolic syndrome can be achieved through dietary changes, with the Mediterranean diet being one effective approach. Overall, metabolic syndrome represents a serious health concern that requires attention to lifestyle and dietary factors to mitigate its associated risks."}{"title": "DYSPLIPIDEMIA:Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal lipid levels in the body. It is often observed in patients with Klinefelter syndrome, a genetic disorder that affects male physical and cognitive development. Management of dyslipidemia typically involves both treatment and dietary modifications to help regulate lipid levels and reduce associated health risks."}{"title": "CANCER OF THE BREAST:Breast cancer is a type of cancer that develops from breast tissue. Research suggests that adherence to the Mediterranean diet may help reduce the risk of developing this disease. Additionally, the risk of breast cancer is associated with hormone replacement therapy, especially when progestogens are included in estrogen treatment."}{"title": "AGRESIVIDAD:La agresividad es un posible efecto secundario del tratamiento con testosterona que debe ser monitoreado durante la terapia."}{"title": "C\u00c9LULAS DE LEYDIG:Las c\u00e9lulas de Leydig son c\u00e9lulas ubicadas en los test\u00edculos que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la producci\u00f3n de testosterona. Estas c\u00e9lulas son estimuladas por la hormona luteinizante (LH) y tambi\u00e9n pueden ser activadas por gonadotropinas. Su funci\u00f3n principal es la s\u00edntesis de testosterona, una hormona esencial para el desarrollo y mantenimiento de caracter\u00edsticas sexuales masculinas."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME METAB\u00d3LICO:The \"S\u00edndrome Metab\u00f3lico\" is a complex cluster of conditions that significantly increases the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes. This syndrome encompasses several interrelated factors, including hypertension, hyperglycemia, excess abdominal fat, and abnormal cholesterol levels. It is often associated with insulin resistance, obesity, and poor nutrition, and can be exacerbated by lifestyle choices such as high salt consumption and the intake of sugar-sweetened beverages and trans fats.\n\nAdditionally, the syndrome may be influenced by dietary factors, including protein and dairy consumption, although evidence regarding the protective effects of dairy is inconsistent. There is also a noted association between the syndrome and conditions such as dislipidemia, hyperuricemia, and kidney stone formation. Furthermore, treatment with testosterone has been identified as a potential exacerbating factor for the syndrome.\n\nOverall, the \"S\u00edndrome Metab\u00f3lico\" represents a significant health concern, necessitating careful dietary management and lifestyle modifications to mitigate its associated risks."}{"title": "SHOX:The SHOX gene is located on the X chromosome and plays a crucial role in determining height. It is particularly significant in patients with Turner syndrome, where its deficiency is commonly associated with the characteristic short stature observed in these individuals."}{"title": "CARDIOPAT\u00cdA ISQU\u00c9MICA:La cardiopat\u00eda isqu\u00e9mica es un riesgo aumentado en mujeres con s\u00edndrome de Turner debido a problemas metab\u00f3licos."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNITARIAS:Las enfermedades autoinmunitarias como la tiroiditis linfoc\u00edtica cr\u00f3nica y la enfermedad cel\u00edaca son m\u00e1s frecuentes en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "FALLO OV\u00c1RICO:El fallo ov\u00e1rico es una condici\u00f3n com\u00fan en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner, caracterizada por gonadotrofinas elevadas y estradiol bajo."}{"title": "MENOPAUSIA PRECOZ:La menopausia precoz es una posible evoluci\u00f3n en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner, especialmente en aquellas que inician la pubertad."}{"title": "ANOMAL\u00cdAS CARDIOVASCULARES:Las anomal\u00edas cardiovasculares son comunes en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner, incluyendo defectos card\u00edacos cong\u00e9nitos."}{"title": "DISECCI\u00d3N DE AORTA:La disecci\u00f3n de aorta es una complicaci\u00f3n grave que puede ocurrir en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner, requiriendo vigilancia estrecha."}{"title": "FENOTIPO FEMENINO:"}{"title": "GONADOBLASTOMA:El gonadoblastoma es un tumor mixto de los cordones sexuales-estroma que puede inducir signos de virilizaci\u00f3n en pacientes j\u00f3venes fenot\u00edpicamente femeninas, especialmente en aquellos con material del cromosoma Y."}{"title": "E2:E2 es una forma de estr\u00f3geno que se encuentra en niveles bajos en pacientes con insuficiencia gonadal, como en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "OXANDROLONA:OXANDROLONA es un f\u00e1rmaco que se utiliza en el contexto del tratamiento de pacientes cr\u00edticos. Se trata de un derivado sint\u00e9tico de la testosterona, que se emplea especialmente en adultos que sufren de quemaduras severas, con el objetivo de aumentar la masa magra y acelerar la cicatrizaci\u00f3n de heridas. Adem\u00e1s, la oxandrolona es un tratamiento recomendado para pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Turner que han comenzado el tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento de manera tard\u00eda y que presentan un pron\u00f3stico de talla final insatisfactorio."}{"title": "GEFFNER ME:Geffner ME es coautor de un estudio sobre la salud cardiometab\u00f3lica en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "FAIENZA MF:Faienza MF es uno de los autores que ha investigado sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "VENTURA A:Ventura A es coautor de un estudio sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "COLUCCI S:Colucci S es coautor de un estudio sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "CAVALLO L:Cavallo L es coautor de un estudio sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "GRANO M:Grano M es coautor de un estudio sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "BRUNETTI G:Brunetti G es coautor de un estudio sobre la fragilidad \u00f3sea en el s\u00edndrome de Turner."}{"title": "DAVIS SM:"}{"title": "TURNER SYNDROME:Turner Syndrome is a chromosomal disorder that primarily affects females. It is characterized by the absence of all or part of a second sex chromosome. This genetic disorder can lead to a range of physical and developmental issues, impacting various aspects of health and growth in affected individuals."}{"title": "ANDROGEN INSENSITIVITY SYNDROME:Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (AIS) is a condition characterized by the body's inability to respond to androgens, which are male hormones. Individuals with this syndrome possess a male (XY) karyotype but develop female physical traits as a result of their resistance to these hormones. Despite having male genetic makeup, the lack of response to androgens leads to the manifestation of female characteristics."}{"title": "HORMONE ANTIM\u00dcLLERIAN:Hormone antim\u00fcllerian is produced by Sertoli cells in the testes and plays a crucial role in male sexual differentiation by inhibiting the development of female reproductive structures."}{"title": "TESTOSTERONE:Testosterone is a steroid hormone that plays a crucial role in the development of male reproductive tissues and secondary sexual characteristics. It is commonly measured in hormonal studies, with elevated levels often noted in patient analyses. In women, testosterone is studied for its effects on conditions such as anorexia nervosa, particularly concerning bone density, and is also assessed to diagnose hyperandrogenism, especially in the context of polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS).\n\nIn medical treatments, testosterone is administered to adult male transsexuals to facilitate virilization and amenorrhea, using various methods including injections and gels. Additionally, it is utilized in the treatment of conditions like Klinefelter syndrome to promote the development of male secondary sexual characteristics. However, testosterone levels may decrease in patients with liver disease, which can lead to metabolic and muscular issues.\n\nFor men with hypogonadism, testosterone therapy is a common treatment, but it necessitates careful evaluation of prostate size, prostate-specific antigen (PSA) levels, and hematocrit before initiation to ensure safety and efficacy."}{"title": "DIHYDROTESTOSTERONE:Dihydrotestosterone (DHT) is a potent androgen that plays a critical role in the development of male characteristics. It is essential for the formation of male external genitalia and the emergence of secondary sexual characteristics. DHT's influence is significant in the overall development of male physical traits, underscoring its importance in male sexual differentiation and maturation."}{"title": "5\u0391-REDUCTASE TYPE 2:5\u03b1-reductase type 2 is an enzyme that converts testosterone into dihydrotestosterone, essential for male genital development."}{"title": "CELLS OF LEYDIG:Cells of Leydig are located in the testes and are responsible for producing testosterone, which is vital for male sexual differentiation."}{"title": "CELLS OF SERTOLI:Cells of Sertoli are found in the testes and support the development of sperm cells and produce hormone antim\u00fcllerian."}{"title": "GENETIC DISORDERS:Genetic disorders encompass a range of conditions caused by abnormalities in genes or chromosomes, affecting physical and developmental traits."}{"title": "ANOMALIES OF SEXUAL DIFFERENTIATION:Anomalies of sexual differentiation refer to a spectrum of congenital conditions that result in discordance between chromosomal, gonadal, and phenotypic sex."}{"title": "CARIOTYPE 46,XY:A karyotype of 46,XY indicates a typical male chromosomal pattern, but can be associated with various disorders affecting sexual development."}{"title": "XY INDIVIDUALS:"}{"title": "GONADAL DYSGENESIS:Gonadal Dysgenesis is a condition characterized by the underdevelopment of gonads, which can lead to various disorders of sexual development."}{"title": "5\u0391-REDUCTASE DEFICIENCY:5\u03b1-Reductase Deficiency is a condition that affects male sexual development, where the body cannot convert testosterone into dihydrotestosterone."}{"title": "PTEN HAMARTOMA SYNDROME:PTEN Hamartoma Syndrome is a rare genetic disorder associated with mutations in the PTEN gene, leading to the development of hamartomas and increased cancer risk."}{"title": "DSD:Developmental Sexual Disorder (DSD) refers to a group of conditions characterized by atypical development of physical sex characteristics. This term encompasses a range of congenital conditions known as Differences of Sex Development (DSD), which involve atypical chromosomal, gonadal, or anatomical sex development. These conditions can manifest in various ways, affecting an individual's physical sex characteristics and overall sexual development."}{"title": "CANCER RISK:Cancer risk encompasses the increased likelihood of developing certain types of cancer due to various factors. In individuals with Disorders of Sex Development (DSD), particularly those with XY karyotypes and specific gonadal conditions, the risk of cancer is notably heightened. Additionally, obesity is recognized as a significant factor that elevates cancer risk. Furthermore, numerous studies have explored how dietary factors, including fish consumption and omega-3 fatty acids, can influence cancer risk, indicating that lifestyle choices may also play a critical role in the likelihood of developing cancer."}{"title": "GONADAL MALIGNANCY:Gonadal malignancy refers to cancer that originates in the gonads, with increased risk associated with certain genetic conditions."}{"title": "HYPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG\u00c9NITA:Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia is a genetic disorder affecting adrenal gland function, leading to hormone imbalances and potential sexual development issues."}{"title": "COSTA EMF:Costa EMF is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "RODRIGUES A DE S:Rodrigues A de S is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "GOMES NL:Gomes NL is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "FARIA JAJ:Faria JAJ is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "NISHI MY:Nishi MY is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "GUERRERO-FERN\u00c1NDEZ J:Guerrero-Fern\u00e1ndez J is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "AZCONA SAN JULI\u00c1N C:Azcona San Juli\u00e1n C is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "BARREIRO CONDE J:Barreiro Conde J is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "BERM\u00daDEZ DE LA VEGA JA:Berm\u00fadez de la Vega JA is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "CARCAVILLA URQU\u00cd A:Carcavilla Urqu\u00ed A is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "CASTA\u00d1O GONZ\u00c1LEZ LA:Casta\u00f1o Gonz\u00e1lez LA is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding anomalies of sexual differentiation."}{"title": "LE\u00d3N NY:Le\u00f3n NY is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding differences of sex development."}{"title": "REYES AP:Reyes AP is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding differences of sex development."}{"title": "HARLEY VR:Harley VR is one of the authors referenced in the literature regarding differences of sex development."}{"title": "NAT REV ENDOCRINOL:Nature Reviews Endocrinology is a journal that published a consensus statement on caring for individuals with differences of sex development."}{"title": "ARCH ENDOCRINOL METAB:Archives of Endocrinology and Metabolism is a journal that published a review on Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome."}{"title": "LANCET DIABETES ENDOCRINOL:Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology is a specialized medical journal dedicated to research in the fields of diabetes and endocrine health. It publishes a wide range of studies, including those focused on non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, exploring its causes and treatment strategies. The journal also addresses topics related to differences in sex development and has published significant research on cardiovascular disease and mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes following bariatric surgery. Through its diverse array of articles, Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology contributes to the advancement of knowledge and understanding in these critical areas of health."}{"title": "AN PEDIATR\u00cdA:Anales de Pediatr\u00eda is a journal that published guidelines on anomalies of sexual differentiation.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DENYS-DRASH:El s\u00edndrome de Denys-Drash es un s\u00edndrome raro que incluye enfermedad renal progresiva, trastorno de la diferenciaci\u00f3n sexual y tumor de Wilms, asociado a mutaciones en el gen WT1."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE SMITH-LEMLI-OPITZ:El s\u00edndrome de Smith-Lemli-Opitz es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo que causa discapacidad intelectual y diversas anomal\u00edas fenot\u00edpicas debido a una anomal\u00eda en la s\u00edntesis del colesterol."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE ANTLEY-BIXLER:El s\u00edndrome de Antley-Bixler es un trastorno que puede derivar de un d\u00e9ficit de lanosterol desmetilasa, causando genitales ambiguos y malformaciones esquel\u00e9ticas en algunos casos."}{"title": "WT1:WT1 es un gen que, cuando presenta mutaciones, est\u00e1 asociado al s\u00edndrome de Denys-Drash y a problemas de diferenciaci\u00f3n sexual."}{"title": "CYP19A1:CYP19A1 is a gene located on chromosome 15q21.2 that encodes the aromatase enzyme, which plays a crucial role in converting androgens into estrogens. Mutations in the CYP19A1 gene can lead to a deficiency of aromatase, a condition that is associated with the Smith-Lemli-Opitz syndrome. This gene's function is essential for the proper balance of sex hormones in the body, and its impairment can have significant implications for hormonal health."}{"title": "CYP51A1:CYP51A1 es un gen que est\u00e1 implicado en el s\u00edndrome de Antley-Bixler, relacionado con la esteroidog\u00e9nesis y genitales ambiguos."}{"title": "AROMATASE:Aromatase is a cytochrome P450 enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of androgens (C21 steroids) into estrogens (C18 steroids)."}{"title": "46,XX:46,XX refers to the typical chromosomal pattern for females, which can be affected by aromatase deficiency leading to sexual differentiation disorders."}{"title": "46,XY:46,XY refers to the typical chromosomal pattern for males, who may also experience symptoms related to aromatase deficiency during puberty."}{"title": "FETOPLACENTARY UNIT:The fetoplacental unit refers to the interaction between the fetus and the placenta, where aromatase plays a crucial role in protecting the fetus from androgens."}{"title": "HYPERGONADOTROPIC HYPOGONADISM:Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism is a condition characterized by elevated gonadotropins and low sex steroid levels, often observed in individuals with aromatase deficiency."}{"title": "HYPOSPADIAS:Hypospadias is a condition that can occur in males with aromatase deficiency, affecting the development of the penis."}{"title": "HIRSUTISM:Hirsutism is characterized by the abnormal growth of terminal hair in women, which is often associated with hormonal imbalances, such as those resulting from aromatase deficiency."}{"title": "ACNE:Acne is a skin condition that can be exacerbated by hormonal changes, including those seen in women with aromatase deficiency during pregnancy."}{"title": "ANDROSTENDIONE:Androstendione is an androgen that can accumulate in individuals with aromatase deficiency, contributing to virilization."}{"title": "HYPERTRICHOSIS:Hypertrichosis is a condition characterized by excessive hair growth that is not androgen-dependent, unlike hirsutism."}{"title": "MIEDLICH SU:Miedlich SU is an author referenced in the context of aromatase deficiency in a male patient in the literature."}{"title": "BONE:Bone is a scientific journal that published a case report and review of the literature on aromatase deficiency."}{"title": "ACHERMANN JC:"}{"title": "HIPERANDROGENISMO:Hyperandrogenism is a condition marked by excessive levels of androgens in the body, which can lead to symptoms such as hirsutism."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE OVARIOS POLIQU\u00cdSTICOS:Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a common cause of hyperandrogenism in women, associated with chronic anovulation and various metabolic issues."}{"title": "TUMOR OV\u00c1RICO:Ovarian tumors can secrete androgens, contributing to hyperandrogenism and resulting in hirsutism in women."}{"title": "CARCINOMA DE SUPRARENAL:Adrenal carcinoma is a rare cancer that can produce androgens, leading to symptoms such as hirsutism."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE 21-HIDROXILASA:21-Hydroxylase deficiency is a genetic disorder that affects adrenal steroid production, leading to excess androgens and symptoms like hirsutism."}{"title": "ESTEROIDES ANABOLIZANTES:Anabolic steroids are synthetic derivatives of testosterone that can lead to increased androgen levels and are associated with hirsutism."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE HIPOANDROGENISMO:Hypoandrogenism syndrome refers to conditions with low androgen levels, which can also be relevant in the context of hirsutism."}{"title": "FERRIMAN-GALLWEY:The Ferriman-Gallwey scale is a clinical tool designed to assess hirsutism in women, providing a systematic method to quantify excessive hair growth. This scale utilizes specific cut-off points to indicate pathological levels of androgenization, allowing healthcare professionals to evaluate the severity of hirsutism based on the amount of hair growth in designated areas of the body."}{"title": "SUPRARENAL GLAND:The suprarenal glands are endocrine glands located above the kidneys that produce hormones including cortisol and androgens."}{"title": "OVARIES:The ovaries are female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones, including estrogen and testosterone."}{"title": "17-OH-PROGESTERONE:17-OH-Progesterone is a steroid hormone involved in the menstrual cycle and is used as a marker in diagnosing conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia."}{"title": "HYPERPLASIA SUPRARENAL CONG\u00c9NITA:Congenital adrenal hyperplasia is a genetic disorder affecting adrenal hormone production, often leading to hyperandrogenism in females."}{"title": "MENARCHE:Menarche is the first occurrence of menstruation in females, marking the onset of reproductive capability."}{"title": "VIRILIZATION:Virilization refers to the development of male physical characteristics in females, often due to elevated androgen levels, and can be a symptom of hyperandrogenism."}{"title": "ANDROGENS:Androgens are male hormones, including testosterone, that are found in both males and females. Elevated levels of androgens can lead to various health conditions, such as hirsutism, which is characterized by excessive hair growth, and virilization, which refers to the development of male physical characteristics in females."}{"title": "FAMILY HISTORY:Family history of congenital adrenal hyperplasia can provide important genetic information for diagnosing hyperandrogenism in women."}{"title": "DHT:La DHT es un metabolito activo de la testosterona que tiene una mayor afinidad por el receptor androg\u00e9nico y es crucial en el desarrollo del hirsutismo."}{"title": "TUMORES DE C\u00c9LULAS DE SERTOLI-LEYDIG:Los tumores de c\u00e9lulas de Sertoli-Leydig son tumores ov\u00e1ricos que pueden causar hiperandrogenismo y hirsutismo."}{"title": "ANOVULACI\u00d3N:La anovulaci\u00f3n es la ausencia de ovulaci\u00f3n, que es una de las principales consecuencias del s\u00edndrome de ovario poliqu\u00edstico."}{"title": "MDTEXT.COM, INC.:MDText.com, Inc. is a publisher based in South Dartmouth, MA, known for providing medical information and guidelines."}{"title": "28-YEAR-OLD PATIENT:A 28-year-old female patient presenting with slowly progressive hirsutism and irregular menstrual cycles, suspected to have PCOS."}{"title": "NATIONAL CENTER FOR BIOTECHNOLOGY INFORMATION:The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is a branch of the National Institutes of Health that provides access to biomedical and genomic information."}{"title": "POLYCYSTIC OVARY SYNDROME:Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a prevalent endocrine disorder that primarily affects women. It is characterized by irregular menstrual cycles, elevated levels of androgens, and the presence of polycystic ovaries, which are enlarged ovaries containing small cysts on their outer edges. This hormonal disorder can lead to a range of metabolic and clinical consequences, impacting women's overall health and well-being."}{"title": "SOUTH DARTMOUTH:"}{"title": "HOMA INDEX:The HOMA index is a method used to estimate insulin resistance and beta-cell function, often elevated in patients with Polycystic Ovary Syndrome."}{"title": "SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME:SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME, specifically obstructive sleep apnea syndrome, is a condition characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep. This disorder can be exacerbated by obesity, which may worsen the severity of the condition. Additionally, sleep apnea syndrome has implications for patients undergoing testosterone treatment, highlighting the need for careful management in individuals affected by this disorder."}{"title": "ERYTHROCYTOSIS:Erythrocytosis is a condition where there is an increase in red blood cells, which can be a potential adverse effect of testosterone treatment."}{"title": "ENDOMETRIAL ATROPHY:Endometrial atrophy is the thinning of the endometrial lining, which can occur as a result of testosterone treatment in transsexual men."}{"title": "HEMBREE WC:Hembree WC is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals regarding the appropriate endocrine interventions for individuals experiencing gender dysphoria."}{"title": "COHEN-KETTENIS PT:Cohen-Kettenis PT is recognized as an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline concerning the endocrine treatment of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria. This guideline serves as a critical resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of gender-dysphoric persons, providing evidence-based recommendations for their treatment."}{"title": "GOOREN L:Gooren L is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, outlining best practices and recommendations for endocrine treatment."}{"title": "HANNEMA SE:Hannema SE is recognized as an author of the Clinical Practice Guideline on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons, published by the Endocrine Society. This guideline provides essential recommendations for the endocrine treatment of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, reflecting Hannema SE's expertise and contribution to this important area of healthcare."}{"title": "MEYER WJ:Meyer WJ is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for the clinical management of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, outlining best practices and recommendations for endocrine treatment."}{"title": "CIPROTERONA:Ciproterona is a medication that is primarily used in hormone therapy for transgender individuals, noted for its antiandrogenic effects. It is recommended that Ciproterona be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "HEMATOCRITO:Hematocrit is a measure of the proportion of blood volume that is occupied by red blood cells, important in assessing cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "APNEAS DEL SUE\u00d1O:Sleep apnea is a sleep disorder characterized by pauses in breathing or periods of shallow breathing during sleep, often associated with obesity and metabolic syndrome."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE \u00daTERO:Uterine cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lining of the uterus, with risk factors that may be influenced by hormonal treatments."}{"title": "MAMOGRAF\u00cdA:Mammography is a diagnostic tool used to screen for breast cancer, important for monitoring health in individuals undergoing hormone therapy."}{"title": "HISTERECTOM\u00cdA:Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, which may be relevant for individuals undergoing gender-affirming surgeries."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO HORMONAL:Hormone therapy refers to the use of hormones in medical treatment, particularly for transgender individuals to align physical characteristics with gender identity."}{"title": "CIE-11:The CIE-11, or Clasificaci\u00f3n Internacional de Enfermedades (International Classification of Diseases), is the 11th revision of a comprehensive classification system designed to categorize diseases and health conditions. It was presented at the World Health Assembly in May 2019 for adoption by Member States. This classification system includes parameters specifically for the evaluation of nutritional status, highlighting its role in assessing various health aspects beyond just diseases."}{"title": "CIE-10:The CIE-10, or Clasificaci\u00f3n Internacional de Enfermedades, 10\u00aa revisi\u00f3n, is a comprehensive coding system utilized for the classification of medical diagnoses and procedures. This system plays a crucial role in categorizing diseases and health-related issues, thereby facilitating data collection and clinical management. The CIE-10 is the 10th revision of the International Classification of Diseases and remains in use until the implementation of the CIE-11. Additionally, the CIE-10 provides updated guidelines for the classification of various conditions, including eating disorders, ensuring a standardized approach to health data across different medical contexts."}{"title": "TRASTORNO DE LA IDENTIDAD SEXUAL:The Trastorno de la identidad sexual refers to disorders of sexual identity classified in the CIE-10."}{"title": "ACETATO DE CIPROTERONA:Acetato de ciproterona is a progestin with anti-androgenic properties commonly used in Europe for transgender women."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTOS CON HORMONAS:Hormone treatments are medical procedures that transgender individuals may undergo to align their physical characteristics with their gender identity."}{"title": "IDENTIDAD DE G\u00c9NERO:Gender identity refers to a person's deeply felt internal experience of gender, which may or may not correspond with the sex assigned at birth."}{"title": "INCONGRUENCIA DE G\u00c9NERO:Gender incongruence is a condition where a person's gender identity does not align with their assigned sex at birth, often leading to distress."}{"title": "TRASTORNO DE LA IDENTIDAD SEXUAL DE LA INFANCIA:This refers to a condition in children where there is a marked incongruence between the child's experienced/expressed gender and the gender assigned at birth."}{"title": "TRANSEXUAL MUJER:"}{"title": "HMG:HMG (human menopausal gonadotropin) is a hormone that can be used in conjunction with hCG for treating cryptorchidism."}{"title": "TESTICULOS CRIPTORQU\u00cdDICOS:Cryptorchid testicles are those that have not descended into the scrotum and may require medical intervention."}{"title": "ATROFIA:ATROFIA refers to the condition characterized by the reduction in size or wasting away of body tissues or organs. In the context of neuropathy, atrophy in the feet and hands can be a symptom associated with disorders that affect copper metabolism. Additionally, atrophy can also pertain to the reduction in size of the testicles, which may occur in cases of cryptorchidism. Thus, ATROFIA encompasses both peripheral atrophy related to neurological conditions and testicular atrophy linked to developmental issues."}{"title": "TORSI\u00d3N TESTICULAR:Testicular torsion is a medical emergency that can occur in undescended testicles, leading to severe complications if not treated promptly."}{"title": "HADZISELIMOVIC:Hadziselimovic is a researcher who authored a debate on hormonal treatment of congenital undescended testes in a medical journal."}{"title": "TAY-SACHS DISEASE:Tay-Sachs disease is a neurodegenerative disorder caused by a deficiency of \u03b2-hexosaminidase A, affecting primarily Ashkenazi Jews."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOGY CONSULTATION:An endocrinology consultation was conducted for a 34-year-old patient referred for evaluation of bilateral gynecomastia."}{"title": "MUSCLE FATIGUE:Muscle fatigue is a significant symptom reported by the patient, indicating increasing difficulty in physical activities."}{"title": "HORMONAL STUDY:A hormonal study was requested to evaluate the patient's hormone levels, including FSH, LH, and testosterone."}{"title": "NEUROLOGY REFERRAL:The patient was referred to neurology for further study based on the findings from the endocrinology consultation."}{"title": "TUMORES TESTICULARES:Tumores testiculares son una categor\u00eda de c\u00e1ncer que afecta a los test\u00edculos, incluyendo seminomas y no seminomas, y son responsables de la mayor\u00eda de los casos de c\u00e1ncer testicular."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE KENNEDY:El s\u00edndrome de Kennedy es una enfermedad rara que afecta a varones, caracterizada por debilidad muscular progresiva y atrofia, causada por una mutaci\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica en el receptor androg\u00e9nico."}{"title": "C\u00c9LULAS DE SERTOLI:Las c\u00e9lulas de Sertoli son c\u00e9lulas en los test\u00edculos que apoyan la producci\u00f3n de esperma, estimuladas por la FSH."}{"title": "CAG:La tripleta CAG es una secuencia gen\u00e9tica que se expande en el s\u00edndrome de Kennedy, causando la enfermedad a trav\u00e9s de la mutaci\u00f3n en el receptor androg\u00e9nico."}{"title": "VIH:VIH (HIV) is a virus that can lead to various health complications in infected individuals, including endocrine and metabolic disorders. Additionally, VIH (HIV) is an infection that may result in the development of Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH) and can influence the response to treatment."}{"title": "NATURE PUBLISHING GROUP IBEROAM\u00c9RICA:Nature Publishing Group Iberoam\u00e9rica is a publishing company that released the referenced work on laboratory diagnostics in endocrinology."}{"title": "ALFAYATE R:Alfayate R is one of the authors of the referenced work on laboratory diagnostics in endocrinology."}{"title": "FAJARDO C:Fajardo C is one of the authors of the referenced work on laboratory diagnostics in endocrinology."}{"title": "GONZ\u00c1LEZ-CLEMENTE JM:Gonz\u00e1lez-Clemente JM is one of the authors of the referenced work on laboratory diagnostics in endocrinology."}{"title": "MATSUMOTO AM:Matsumoto AM is the editor of the referenced work on male hypogonadism."}{"title": "J STEROID BIOCHEM MOL BIOL:J Steroid Biochem Mol Biol is a journal that published research on the assessment of free testosterone concentration."}{"title": "HIV-INFECTED WOMEN:HIV-infected women experience various health issues, including amenorrhea and early menopause, as discussed in the text."}{"title": "ESTEROIDES ANDROG\u00c9NICOS:Esteroides androg\u00e9nicos (anabolic steroids) can influence SHBG levels and testosterone availability in the body."}{"title": "MENOPAUSIA TEMPRANA:Menopausia temprana (early menopause) is a condition that can occur in women with HIV and is associated with hormonal changes."}{"title": "GENE SRY:The SRY gene is crucial for male sex determination and is often translocated in individuals with atypical chromosomal patterns."}{"title": "AUDIOLOGICAL ASSESSMENT:Audiological assessments are recommended for patients with 46,XX karyotype due to the frequent occurrence of sensorineural hearing loss."}{"title": "AZOOSPERMIA:Azoospermia is a medical condition characterized by the absence of sperm in the semen, commonly found in individuals with Klinefelter syndrome."}{"title": "MICROCEFALIA:Microcefalia is a condition where a person's head is significantly smaller than expected, which can be associated with genetic syndromes including Klinefelter syndrome."}{"title": "CARDIOPAT\u00cdAS:Cardiopat\u00edas refer to heart diseases that may be present in individuals with certain genetic conditions, including Klinefelter syndrome."}{"title": "MENOPAUSE:"}{"title": "GEN SRY:The SRY gene is involved in the differentiation of Sertoli cells and the development of testicles, crucial for male sexual development."}{"title": "AZF:The AZF region is a genetic factor associated with azoospermia, which is the absence of sperm in semen, affecting male fertility."}71␀␀␀␀␀Å81␀␀␀␀␀'91␀␀␀␀␀ƒ91␀␀␀␀␀<1␀␀␀␀␀¬<1␀␀␀␀␀f=1␀␀␀␀␀˜=1␀␀␀␀␀«?1␀␀␀␀␀LA1␀␀␀␀␀ﬁB1␀␀␀␀␀nC1␀␀␀␀␀˛C1␀␀␀␀␀F1␀␀␀␀␀ÓF1␀␀␀␀␀ΩG1␀␀␀␀␀òH1␀␀␀␀␀gI1␀␀␀␀␀<J1␀␀␀␀␀K1␀␀␀␀␀ÌK1␀␀␀␀␀‚L1␀␀␀␀␀wM1␀␀␀␀␀ÊO1␀␀␀␀␀≈Q1␀␀␀␀␀óR1␀␀␀␀␀dS1␀␀␀␀␀T1␀␀␀␀␀œU1␀␀␀␀␀XV1␀␀␀␀␀W1␀␀␀␀␀∫W1␀␀␀␀␀NX1␀␀␀␀␀FY1␀␀␀␀␀\\1␀␀␀␀␀A_1␀␀␀␀␀X`1␀␀␀␀␀4a1␀␀␀␀␀Óa1␀␀␀␀␀!f1␀␀␀␀␀Yh1␀␀␀␀␀i1␀␀␀␀␀jj1␀␀␀␀␀él1␀␀␀␀␀£m1␀␀␀␀␀©n1␀␀␀␀␀ûr1␀␀␀␀␀ás1␀␀␀␀␀}v1␀␀␀␀␀˛z1␀␀␀␀␀T{1␀␀␀␀␀Ø~1␀␀␀␀␀œ1␀␀␀␀␀<Ä1␀␀␀␀␀eÄ1␀␀␀␀␀1Å1␀␀␀␀␀ˇÅ1␀␀␀␀␀LÖ1␀␀␀␀␀Ü1␀␀␀␀␀Óà1␀␀␀␀␀râ1␀␀␀␀␀<ä1␀␀␀␀␀ﬂä1␀␀␀␀␀Òã1␀␀␀␀␀Ôç1␀␀␀␀␀é1␀␀␀␀␀öé1␀␀␀␀␀Cè1␀␀␀␀␀␀ê1␀␀␀␀␀†ë1␀␀␀␀␀6í1␀␀␀␀␀Xí1␀␀␀␀␀ôï1␀␀␀␀␀Bñ1␀␀␀␀␀¯ñ1␀␀␀␀␀yô1␀␀␀␀␀¬õ1␀␀␀␀␀˜ù1␀␀␀␀␀∞†1␀␀␀␀␀n°1␀␀␀␀␀â°1␀␀␀␀␀/¢1␀␀␀␀␀Õ¢1␀␀␀␀␀å£1␀␀␀␀␀á•1␀␀␀␀␀?®1␀␀␀␀␀!©1␀␀␀␀␀Ë©1␀␀␀␀␀»≠1␀␀␀␀␀ïÆ1␀␀␀␀␀_Ø1␀␀␀␀␀7∞1␀␀␀␀␀È∞1␀␀␀␀␀ø±1␀␀␀␀␀Ê±1␀␀␀␀␀:¥1␀␀␀␀␀Ë∂1␀␀␀␀␀–∑1␀␀␀␀␀û∏1␀␀␀␀␀3ª1␀␀␀␀␀„ª1␀␀␀␀␀ïæ1␀␀␀␀␀Wø1␀␀␀␀␀¿1␀␀␀␀␀¡1␀␀␀␀␀A√1␀␀␀␀␀Ωƒ1␀␀␀␀␀W≈1␀␀␀␀␀‚«1␀␀␀␀␀Ö»1␀␀␀␀␀Q…1␀␀␀␀␀(À1␀␀␀␀␀␀Ã1␀␀␀␀␀ÎÕ1␀␀␀␀␀‰œ1␀␀␀␀␀ö—1␀␀␀␀␀M“1␀␀␀␀␀^”1␀␀␀␀␀é‘1␀␀␀␀␀⁄’1␀␀␀␀␀E◊1␀␀␀␀␀˘◊1␀␀␀␀␀»ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀ïŸ1␀␀␀␀␀©€1␀␀␀␀␀i‹1␀␀␀␀␀jﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀%ﬂ1␀␀␀␀␀¿‡1␀␀␀␀␀c·1␀␀␀␀␀␀‚1␀␀␀␀␀ç„1␀␀␀␀␀cÊ1␀␀␀␀␀=Á1␀␀␀␀␀ﬂÎ1␀␀␀␀␀wÓ1␀␀␀␀␀Ô1␀␀␀␀␀÷Ô1␀␀␀␀␀.Ú1␀␀␀␀␀OÙ1␀␀␀␀␀íı1␀␀␀␀␀ˆ1␀␀␀␀␀õˆ1␀␀␀␀␀D¯1␀␀␀␀␀‹¯1␀␀␀␀␀7¸1␀␀␀␀␀ˆ¸1␀␀␀␀␀´˝1␀␀␀␀␀R˛1␀␀␀␀␀ˇ1␀␀␀␀␀≠ˇ1␀␀␀␀␀A␀2␀␀␀␀␀Ò␀2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀ˇ2␀␀␀␀␀Ã2␀␀␀␀␀Ö2␀␀␀␀␀'2␀␀␀␀␀Æ2␀␀␀␀␀b2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀ª2␀␀␀␀␀ç	2␀␀␀␀␀#
